{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong","id":967358,"title":"Magick question: \"What happens when the consensus is WRONG?\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-11T09:21:59-07:00","id":967358,"title":"Magick question: \"What happens when the consensus is WRONG?\"","content":"Background on me: I love Mage, or at least the idea of it... but back when I started WoD, my troupe found the 2E magick system too complex and with too many unanswered (IMPORTANT) questions to ever practically play it. So we never did. Now, 2 editions later, I'm seeing people here intelligently debate and quote books on topics that had everyone walking away in a huff before... so I thought I'd start asking. (I'll divide them into separate threads to try and avoid making this a mess)<br /> <br /> The actual question: <br /> <br /> Consensual reality and the notion of &quot;Would an onlooker see this as impossible?&quot; seem to be the major players in what's Coincidental and Vulgar in Mage.... so what happens when:<br /> <br /> 1) The effect is totally plausible, but there's no way any onlooker (hypothetical or otherwise) would have the knowledge/omniscience to KNOW it's plausible. Sudden aneurysms, a bare wire somewhere buried in the walls making something elsewhere electrified, or any effect where a background in science or intense googling would be required to know it's actually a thing that happens. There might be a perfectly scientific explanation (or method used) for Mark Patsy to suddenly drop dead while walking down the street... but does that make it coincidental? If so, or if that's accepted as a thing that CAN happen, does the Mage even NEED a convoluted method or explanation to kill that way?<br /> <br /> 2) The effect is actually scientifically possible, but due to poor education or common misconception most people would think that the opposite, or something completely different would happen. Like INCREASING the concentration of a flammable gas so it snuffs out its own flame (due to lack of oxygen mix), making water pure so it won't conduct electricity, or using concrete as a conduit path of your own electrical attack.<br /> <br /> 3) Something is impossible, but due to poor education or common misconception most people think that's the way it happens. Best example is the belief a penny dropped off the Empire State can kill someone or embed itself inches into concrete, rather than not even being able to leave a bruise. (Of course the Mythbusters probably had an impact on this one, but until then I think most folks accepted it as fact)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T09:45:38-07:00","id":967369,"title":"","content":"The short answer is that the Consensus is never wrong. Consensus determines reality and any &quot;But scientifically it actually works this way.&quot; is in fact a technocratic project actively meant to ALTER that consensus and thus alter reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T10:05:57-07:00","id":967379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong#post967358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) The effect is totally plausible, but there's no way any onlooker (hypothetical or otherwise) would have the knowledge/omniscience to KNOW it's plausible. Sudden aneurysms, a bare wire somewhere buried in the walls making something elsewhere electrified, or any effect where a background in science or intense googling would be required to know it's actually a thing that happens. There might be a perfectly scientific explanation (or method used) for Mark Patsy to suddenly drop dead while walking down the street... but does that make it coincidental? If so, or if that's accepted as a thing that CAN happen, does the Mage even NEED a convoluted method or explanation to kill that way?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would depend on the circumstances. Once Maybe. A Mage runs up to 5 people and shouts curses at them and then they all drop dead.. not so much.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) The effect is actually scientifically possible, but due to poor education or common misconception most people would think that the opposite, or something completely different would happen. Like INCREASING the concentration of a flammable gas so it snuffs out its own flame (due to lack of oxygen mix), making water pure so it won't conduct electricity, or using concrete as a conduit path of your own electrical attack. </div> </div> </div>Conincidental.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Something is impossible, but due to poor education or common misconception most people think that's the way it happens. Best example is the belief a penny dropped off the Empire State can kill someone or embed itself inches into concrete, rather than not even being able to leave a bruise. (Of course the Mythbusters probably had an impact on this one, but until then I think most folks accepted it as fact) </div> </div> </div>Conincidental<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T10:06:49-07:00","id":967380,"title":"","content":"If you are in an area where, due to bad education or misunderstandings or even real world experience, people believe something different than the general consensus, you are in a different reality zone. The rules really are different. How many people it takes for that to happen is up to the ST, but it can happen. In Mage, in the deepest reaches of the jungle, your smartphone, your watch, and possibly even your gun <i>could</i> stop working. <br /> <br /> Also, remember that often the reasons why something can happen are unimportant, what's important is just that people think something can happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T10:47:16-07:00","id":967402,"title":"","content":"As stated above, Science as we know it in Real Life is, in MtAs, just one of many equally valid Paradigms for Reality. Indeed, &quot;Science&quot; is kind of a loose term, and what's seen as scientific fact has changed radically over millennia. The ancient Greek natural philosophers were convinced of the primacy of the four classical elements, and that unicorns really existed (it wasn't the myth-makers that wrote about them, but the <i>naturalists</i>). Medieval doctors and researchers talked at length about humorism, and performed long calculations to track the paths of planets, assuming a geocentric model. As late as the nineteenth century, substances like the Luminiferous Ether, Miasma, and Phlogiston were ardently defended by the scientific consensus. It would be arrogant of us modern thinkers to presume that we now have a completely &quot;correct&quot; grasp of how the world works, and that subsequent years won't see long-held &quot;facts&quot; overturned (and then seen by future men and women as quaint concepts).<br /> <br /> Now imagine that no aspect of Science is set in stone, but is based entirely on the ability of thinkers to convince other people of a theory's viability. Imagine that things like Darwinian Evolution became exploitable facts (for Technomancers), simply because it became massively popular in the public consciousness.<br /> <br /> When it comes to Mage and coincidence, the important question is not &quot;does Science support this?&quot;, but rather &quot;does popular belief support this?&quot;. If enough people in a given area believe that glass is actually a very slow-moving liquid (rather than a solid crystal), a Mage could possibly manipulate glass like a fluid and have it be coincidental. On the other hand, most people don't realize that flammable gases need a certain concentration of oxygen to ignite; they assume that if it's flammable, that's all that's needed for a combustion reaction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:03:29-07:00","id":967410,"title":"","content":"Of course this means all those 'breast cancer awareness' events we see IRL are actually INCREASING the amount of breast cancer that exists. Rather than solving it.<br /> <br /> Breast Cancer Awareness is a Nephandic plot!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:18:13-07:00","id":967416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=967369#post967369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The short answer is that the Consensus is never wrong. Consensus determines reality and any &quot;But scientifically it actually works this way.&quot; is in fact a technocratic project actively meant to ALTER that consensus and thus alter reality.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not true, mage has a concept known as &quot;earthly foundations&quot;, things the consensus can not and will not effect. For instance, gravity has existed long before isaac newton discovered it and no amount of people believing otherwise can make it stop working. It is only the huboris of mages that makes them believe humans command All of reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:22:08-07:00","id":967420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=967416#post967416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not true, mage has a concept known as &quot;earthly foundations&quot;, things the consensus can not and will not effect. For instance, gravity has existed long before isaac newton discovered it and no amount of people believing otherwise can make it stop working. It is only the huboris of mages that makes them believe humans command All of reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changing Gravity is difficult but not outside the bounds of Awakened Magic. And thus, not outside the bounds of the Consensus.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T13:00:53-07:00","id":967476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=967416#post967416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not true, mage has a concept known as &quot;earthly foundations&quot;, things the consensus can not and will not effect. For instance, gravity has existed long before isaac newton discovered it and no amount of people believing otherwise can make it stop working. It is only the huboris of mages that makes them believe humans command All of reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Newton may have categorized it and defined it, and in Mage terms he might have even altered the way it worked. There's no indication that gravity didn't exist in some form before him. People believed in it even if they didn't know how it worked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T13:41:55-07:00","id":967509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=967420#post967420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changing Gravity is difficult but not outside the bounds of Awakened Magic. And thus, not outside the bounds of the Consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the concept of cosmological constants/earthly foundations is poorly defined and how mages exalt their own legends, it's more of a &quot;golden rule&quot; subject. Whether the consensus is god and Anything that humanity believes is right, or mages are arrogant pricks who can't accept that humanity isn't the center of the universe is up to you.<br /> <br /> I tend to believe the latter, as it also is in line with the theme of how mages use magic to begin with. They all use the same magic, but refuse to believe it because their magic is &quot;obviously the right way to use magic&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T13:55:46-07:00","id":967514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=967476#post967476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Newton may have categorized it and defined it, and in Mage terms he might have even altered the way it worked. There's no indication that gravity didn't exist in some form before him. People believed in it even if they didn't know how it worked.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This brings the question how would the world (physics) be if there were no humand beings to create consensus?<br /> <br /> Personally, I think not everything is resultof consensus, so no &quot;more breast cancer&quot; because people start believing in it.<br /> <br /> About the questions of OP, I'd say every of them is coincident. To be vulgar it must be a &quot;WTF?!?&quot; situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T14:25:05-07:00","id":967523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=967514#post967514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This brings the question how would the world (physics) be if there were no humand beings to create consensus?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's *exactly* what the &quot;Earthly Foundations&quot; are about.<br /> They are the parts of reality that existed before humanity ever entered the scene. Gravity, light, sound, matter, fire, life, the flow of time, electricity in the form of thunderstorms.<br /> Such things. They are not made up by the consensus.<br /> <br /> Now, while the Consensus can not get *rid* of those things or change their basic behavior on a global scale, nor change what they cause, what the Consensus CAN do is define how those things actually come to be. Electrons? Elemental spirits? Will of the Gods? *That's* still mallable (And the Technocracy is of course pressing the classic physics and chemistry angles), but you cannot change the fact that the Earthly Foundations exist. Not permanently, and even temporarily would be goddamn hard. That's Archmage Sphere level 10 stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-11-2016, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T17:06:38-07:00","id":967613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=967514#post967514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This brings the question how would the world (physics) be if there were no humand beings to create consensus?<br /> <br /> Personally, I think not everything is resultof consensus, so no &quot;more breast cancer&quot; because people start believing in it.<br /> <br /> About the questions of OP, I'd say every of them is coincident. To be vulgar it must be a &quot;WTF?!?&quot; situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fundamental problem with attributing cancer to earthly foundations is that cancer is a disease that only makes sense in a medical paradigm that includes genetics and cellular structures. Generic wasting diseases could exist in a paradigm revolving around evil spirits or humors, but their behavior (and in some cases intelligence) would be so different they can't possibly be the same thing.<br /> <br /> This is actually a major problem with Earthly Foundations, and why I rely on them as little as possible.<br /> <br /> Classic Mage Questions: Was the earth flat before the Ancient Greeks proved it was round? Did the sun revolve around the earth until Copernicus and Galileo brought their maths to everyone's attention? And in general the idea is that, yes, the consensus really can shape the world to that degree. At one point, heavier things did fall faster than slower things. At one point the planets were pushed around by angels.<br /> <br /> But what does that mean for the concept of gravity? On a flat world gravity is a generic unidirectional tendency in one direction. On a geocentric one, it is a universal pull towards a central point (one that only affects earth, given that angels need to push the planets around). In Newton's model it's a general attraction of mass to mass. In one I'm always falling towards earth, unless I get beneath it, in which case I'm falling away. In one I'm falling towards the center of the universe, but not everything is. In one everything behaves the same way, but I can be pulled in any direction depending on where I am.<br /> <br /> An Earthly Foundation of &quot;Things are affected by a downward force&quot; seems a pretty arbitrary universal rule when we can completely change the definition of &quot;down,&quot; &quot;force,&quot; and &quot;things.&quot;<br /> <br /> I prefer to think of it this way. We live for so long in an environment where things fall downward that it is deeply written into our expectations, in a way that things like cars and gunpowder and germs just aren't. We learn to account for gravity and light and matter before we even learn to speak. They are consequently next to impossible to convince the consensus to fully abandon in any kind of straightforward way. It's not an arbitrary set of universal constants at work, its just a massive amount of conceptual inertia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T20:10:01-07:00","id":967698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=967523#post967523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, while the Consensus can not get *rid* of those things or change their basic behavior on a global scale, nor change what they cause, what the Consensus CAN do is define how those things actually come to be. Electrons? Elemental spirits? Will of the Gods? *That's* still mallable (And the Technocracy is of course pressing the classic physics and chemistry angles), but you cannot change the fact that the Earthly Foundations exist. Not permanently, and even temporarily would be goddamn hard. That's Archmage Sphere level 10 stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would contest this, actually, depending on how 'basic' you mean by 'basic behavior'. While &quot;things fall down&quot; is certainly a constant, and the behavior of most things near the Earth's surface is as well (and reinforced by direct human experience), the actual <i>behavior</i> away from the most commonly encountered situations are... highly variable, and not just in 'what causes this'.<br /> <br /> For instance, Newtonian and Einsteinian gravity models both describe the gravitational force such that in some places, <i>there is no down for things to fall</i>. Places far away from Earth's surface, sure, but places nonetheless - where the forces balance out to exactly zero. That means that the force can in a sense 'not exist' in places. And these places are different for the different theories and models. Likewise, how much fall things undergo is likewise variable.<br /> <br /> Also, they define a zero-gravity-point in the center of the Earth, so it's not <i>quite</i> as... solely unEarthly as might be expected.<br /> <br /> So, if both those models, and many others - respecting the 'things which are heavyish on Earth act this way' constraint - can be true based on Consensus, then Consensus can actually get very close to altering the 'basic' behavior of these constants in a lot of ways, so long as certain particular global constraints are respected.<br /> <br /> These global constraints are probably the <i>true</i> constants, unlike the possibly-deceptive labels of &quot;gravity&quot; and so on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I blame Autochthon. Stupid Loom of Fate, making the core Creation reality infrastructure so robust.[/lolcrossovers]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-11-2016, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T21:02:40-07:00","id":967728,"title":"","content":"Most people believe the scientific consensus, even if they don't understand it. The scientific consensus may not determine the overall Consensus, especially at its edges, but it's certainly one of the biggest influences. I think it has enough momentum to carry reality past some occasional incredulity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T21:18:08-07:00","id":967737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=967728#post967728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most people believe the scientific consensus, even if they don't understand it. The scientific consensus may not determine the overall Consensus, especially at its edges, but it's certainly one of the biggest influences. I think it has enough momentum to carry reality past some occasional incredulity.</div> </div> </div> </div>to the point you can pull off coincidences via &quot;sciencey bullshit&quot; if you're not near a specialist that <b>knows</b> thermodynamics doesn't allow that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T21:21:46-07:00","id":967740,"title":"","content":"I generally have used science as the foundation reality and magic as an overlay that temporarily alters reality. The spiritual planes have their own form of science as the foundational reality and, in order to change their reality, magic must be used to overlay their reality. The Consensus is nothing more than the deluded hubris of Mages who are trying to permanently change the laws of reality in vain to avoid having to use magic. Linear magic is explicitly scientific, even if human science is incapable of explaining it, because it can be used without altering reality. Coincidental magic involves subtle alterations in reality while vulgar magic involves obvious alterations in reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T21:22:25-07:00","id":967741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=967698#post967698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would contest this, actually, depending on how 'basic' you mean by 'basic behavior'. While &quot;things fall down&quot; is certainly a constant, and the behavior of most things near the Earth's surface is as well (and reinforced by direct human experience), the actual <i>behavior</i> away from the most commonly encountered situations are... highly variable, and not just in 'what causes this'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's the basic behavior I meant <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Gravity = things fall down.<br /> Fire = Hot burnination<br /> Time = You know, goes forward, not backward.<br /> <br /> Really, down to the simplest description of the thing. There can be *Local* anomalies of course, but that's how they work overall since before man.<br /> Also, of course, the Earthly Foundations are *Earthly* foundations, not Tellurian Foundations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Classic Mage Questions: Was the earth flat before the Ancient Greeks proved it was round? Did the sun revolve around the earth until Copernicus and Galileo brought their maths to everyone's attention? And in general the idea is that, yes, the consensus really can shape the world to that degree. At one point, heavier things did fall faster than slower things. At one point the planets were pushed around by angels.<br /> <br /> But what does that mean for the concept of gravity? On a flat world gravity is a generic unidirectional tendency in one direction. On a geocentric one, it is a universal pull towards a central point (one that only affects earth, given that angels need to push the planets around). </div> </div> </div>But in either case it means 'Stuff falls down to the ground' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> For an arbitrary overall shape of the earth. Also note that, as I said above, it's Earthly Foundations. As soon as you leave earth, all bets are off and..well. As Mage describes, the Consensus is doing a number on Earth's surroundings. Cosmologically, that area is outside the borders of the shard realm that Earth makes up. 'Earth Realm Foundations' would have been the better name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-12-2016, 12:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T21:52:33-07:00","id":967756,"title":"","content":"You know, adding to that, I think I found the best analogy for the 'Earthly Foundations'.<br /> <br /> The Earthly Foundations are the same thing as the very simplest, basic rules that you put in place when making the shell of a Horizon Realm, before tossing in life, forces and matter and letting it brew. Or shaping it, depending on how you go about it.<br /> Which, of course, usually are quite close to the normal Earthly Foundations because the human animals called Mages just prefer for things to work in similar ways.<br /> <br /> If Horizon Realms didn't have their own Foundations, a pile of Mages living in them would wreak havoc. The difference is that changing those foundations in locally restricted areas is usually not against such a realm's Consensus. But trying to remove them from a realm probably hits you with the same barriers.<br /> <br /> ...of course this puts up interesting ideas and possibilities about Earth's origin itself...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-12-2016, 01:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T05:23:50-07:00","id":967866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=967741#post967741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But in either case it means 'Stuff falls down to the ground' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> For an arbitrary overall shape of the earth. Also note that, as I said above, it's Earthly Foundations. As soon as you leave earth, all bets are off and..well. As Mage describes, the Consensus is doing a number on Earth's surroundings. Cosmologically, that area is outside the borders of the shard realm that Earth makes up. 'Earth Realm Foundations' would have been the better name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or away from the ground, if you happen to be living on a flat earth and fall over the edge.<br /> <br /> It's that &quot;stuff falls to the ground&quot; expectation that makes me think it's a deeply ingrained product of the consensus and not a fundamental rule of earth. It's behavior is only consistent from the point of view of people standing on the typical surface. From any other viewpoint, even those within Earth's domain, the rule varies wildly. Mage is a humanistic game, so I'll concede that it is plausible that the fundamental rules of earth are oddly directed towards the realms humans would normally go to. That said, it is considerably simpler to look to the consensus as the source of any kind of subjective rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T06:01:08-07:00","id":967878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=967613#post967613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fundamental problem with attributing cancer to earthly foundations is that cancer is a disease that only makes sense in a medical paradigm that includes genetics and cellular structures. Generic wasting diseases could exist in a paradigm revolving around evil spirits or humors, but their behavior (and in some cases intelligence) would be so different they can't possibly be the same thing.<br /> <br /> This is actually a major problem with Earthly Foundations, and why I rely on them as little as possible.<br /> <br /> Classic Mage Questions: Was the earth flat before the Ancient Greeks proved it was round? Did the sun revolve around the earth until Copernicus and Galileo brought their maths to everyone's attention? And in general the idea is that, yes, the consensus really can shape the world to that degree. At one point, heavier things did fall faster than slower things. At one point the planets were pushed around by angels.<br /> <br /> But what does that mean for the concept of gravity? On a flat world gravity is a generic unidirectional tendency in one direction. On a geocentric one, it is a universal pull towards a central point (one that only affects earth, given that angels need to push the planets around). In Newton's model it's a general attraction of mass to mass. In one I'm always falling towards earth, unless I get beneath it, in which case I'm falling away. In one I'm falling towards the center of the universe, but not everything is. In one everything behaves the same way, but I can be pulled in any direction depending on where I am.<br /> <br /> An Earthly Foundation of &amp;quot;Things are affected by a downward force&amp;quot; seems a pretty arbitrary universal rule when we can completely change the definition of &amp;quot;down,&amp;quot; &amp;quot;force,&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;things.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I prefer to think of it this way. We live for so long in an environment where things fall downward that it is deeply written into our expectations, in a way that things like cars and gunpowder and germs just aren't. We learn to account for gravity and light and matter before we even learn to speak. They are consequently next to impossible to convince the consensus to fully abandon in any kind of straightforward way. It's not an arbitrary set of universal constants at work, its just a massive amount of conceptual inertia.</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly disagree entitely with what you posted. And I believe there is no where in the books to base your statrments, if there are, I'm sorry and I'd like to see it.<br /> <br /> As I understand the consensus isn't reality per se. Consensus is what most people in an area believe exist/is possible, making those things doable without reality hitting you back. This doesn't mean consensus shape the universe. <br /> <br /> To me, the universe has his own laws, people believing that you can reverse gravity just makes it easy yo reverse, not make it reverse. People believing in breast cancer make it possible for someone with Life to give breast cancer to someone without getting paradox, it doesn't mean that it wouldn't exist if they didn't believe.<br /> <br /> Saying that the earth was flat before people believed it was round is extreme. Changing the shape of a planet is a planetary feat that would have lots of consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T08:32:41-07:00","id":967944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=967878#post967878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I strongly disagree entitely with what you posted. And I believe there is no where in the books to base your statrments, if there are, I'm sorry and I'd like to see it.<br /> <br /> As I understand the consensus isn't reality per se. Consensus is what most people in an area believe exist/is possible, making those things doable without reality hitting you back. This doesn't mean consensus shape the universe.<br /> <br /> To me, the universe has his own laws, people believing that you can reverse gravity just makes it easy yo reverse, not make it reverse. People believing in breast cancer make it possible for someone with Life to give breast cancer to someone without getting paradox, it doesn't mean that it wouldn't exist if they didn't believe.<br /> <br /> Saying that the earth was flat before people believed it was round is extreme. Changing the shape of a planet is a planetary feat that would have lots of consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would it be extreme? When the medical view of the four humors was overturned was there a massive expultion of blood, bile, and phlegm from every body in existence, or did the world just tick on behaving much the way people expected it to? <br /> <br /> It's one of those oddities of Mage. It seems like fundamental shifts to the rules of the world should be accompanied by visible uphevals and disasters, but they aren't because the sleepers don't think anything actually changed.<br /> <br /> I see the temptation to take that kind of power away from the consensus, but I think it's damaging to the core conceits of Mage. Yes, we want a world that's going to stay mostly like our own, but we also shouldn't undercut the reasons Mages are fighting over the Consensus in the first place. It really is that powerful; it can reshape the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T08:53:14-07:00","id":967958,"title":"","content":"Philosophers struggle since ages to get answers to varying metaphysic questions. In Mage you can decide (as ST or as troupe) that only things that are perceived (directly or indirectly) are real. <br /> <br /> You can decide that time flows backward and is only perceived to flow onward.<br /> <br /> And other things.<br /> <br /> My reading of mage was, is and will be, that magi have active control over their reality bending powers, sleepers do not. But sleepers can nonetheless bend reality to their collective will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T09:21:48-07:00","id":967978,"title":"","content":"I think that before we had science and explanations for why things are the way they are, there wasn't really a why. When you swim in water, you can go up and down because you're surrounded by water - a thing you can drink, hold up, touch, etc. When you're in air, there's nothing to &quot;touch&quot; in the same way or meaningfully interact with - so it's not &quot;solid&quot; enough to contain you. You are near to the ground because that's what makes sense intuitively. In essence, there was no gravity, just an expectation of staying near the ground.<br /> <br /> What would life be like if it was more &quot;narrative&quot; rather than objective? Maybe a journey to find your new homeland would be a hard journey, fraught with cliffs and hills and barren wastes, not because you happen to be traversing a geographic area with past tectonic activity and an arid climate, but because you expect a journey to uproot your life and change everything about it *should* be hard? How would things change when someone comes up with the idea that the difficulty of a journey depends not on why you're taking the journey but the nature of the path you're taking?<br /> <br /> Part of the modern world is this air of superiority when we look at history - how amazed we are that they lived how they lived, unaware of the scientific reality all around them. I think Mage is more fun when we explicitly discard that perspective. No, your laptop doesn't work in the deep Amazonian jungle. Yes, there were dragons long ago that needed to be slain. No, Dark Ages Europeans aren't stupid for not inventing gunpowder like the Chinese; it wasn't possible to make it there and then. When things were invented, they were *created*.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T10:53:37-07:00","id":968016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=967944#post967944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would it be extreme? When the medical view of the four humors was overturned was there a massive expultion of blood, bile, and phlegm from every body in existence, or did the world just tick on behaving much the way people expected it to? <br /> <br /> It's one of those oddities of Mage. It seems like fundamental shifts to the rules of the world should be accompanied by visible uphevals and disasters, but they aren't because the sleepers don't think anything actually changed.<br /> <br /> I see the temptation to take that kind of power away from the consensus, but I think it's damaging to the core conceits of Mage. Yes, we want a world that's going to stay mostly like our own, but we also shouldn't undercut the reasons Mages are fighting over the Consensus in the first place. It really is that powerful; it can reshape the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how it works. The universe and the planet are way older than human race. All the laws of physics were already concretized. What human beings can do is alter that laws through pure will, just like you can alter your bedroom color with paint, but instead of bedroom it's the universe laws and instead of paint it's the Mage will. The consensus simply makes it easier to paint, like giving you a brush.<br /> <br /> The universe isn't the consensus, consensus is simply how easy it is to CHANGE the laws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T11:31:14-07:00","id":968043,"title":"","content":"Yes, I think that the Changing Breeds would remember when the Earth was flat, since they predate Mages by a minimum of 250 million years. I think that the Consensus is merely the store of available energy to reshape local reality. The Americas existed before European Mages decided that it would be a fine idea to commit genocide against the Native Americans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T12:53:03-07:00","id":968087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=968016#post968016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not how it works. The universe and the planet are way older than human race. All the laws of physics were already concretized. What human beings can do is alter that laws through pure will, just like you can alter your bedroom color with paint, but instead of bedroom it's the universe laws and instead of paint it's the Mage will. The consensus simply makes it easier to paint, like giving you a brush.<br /> <br /> The universe isn't the consensus, consensus is simply how easy it is to CHANGE the laws.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a lot of assumptions, and I'm not sure we need to make them. In fact, some of them are wrong. <br /> <br /> The majority of the universe is the Deep Universe/Deep Umbra, and it has no rules. Everything is coincidental out there. There isn't a one true set of physics out there that anyone has been able to determine. <br /> <br /> As for the planet, sure, that could be older than humans. It's at least as plausible an idea in Mage as humans being older than earth. But is it older than Avatars? Is it older than Pure Ones? Is it older than forces that can change reality? Were the rules ever concrete, or were they chosen by Will all the way down?<br /> <br /> And even if there is some arbitrary baseline set of rules, you're not saying how they keep the consensus from changing the shape of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T14:37:47-07:00","id":968147,"title":"","content":"Yes, yes, and yes. Gaia is older than humans, Gaia is older than the Avatars, and Gaia is older than the Pure Ones. Heck, the Changing Breeds are older than humans, Avatars, and Pure Ones because they were created by Gaia (or one of her subordinates).<br /> <br /> Imagine Reality as an acre of land, the Consensus as the materials to build a house, and the Mage as the builder. The better the Mage, the better the house, but they cannot really do anything to change the size of the land and the type of house that they can build is limited by the available materials. Now, do you complain about only having an acre of land or do you just build the best house that you can with the available resources?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T15:29:42-07:00","id":968186,"title":"","content":"Part of the fun of playing mage is that you can take mutually exclusive sides in a given controversy and both of you are right(and wrong of course) at the same time.<br /> <br /> All your troubles answering smooth questions like this go away if you simply aknowledge:<br /> There is no absolute truth (in mage).<br /> <br /> Gaia can be the oldest entity in the Tellurian.<br /> Logos can be the oldest entity in the Tellurian.<br /> I can be the oldest entity in the Tellurian.<br /> <br /> It enriches the game if no objective truth is set.<br /> At least not for the players.<br /> If it where not so, then we would not engage in this conversation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T18:52:12-07:00","id":968302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=968087#post968087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a lot of assumptions, and I'm not sure we need to make them. In fact, some of them are wrong.<br /> <br /> The majority of the universe is the Deep Universe/Deep Umbra, and it has no rules. Everything is coincidental out there. There isn't a one true set of physics out there that anyone has been able to determine.<br /> <br /> As for the planet, sure, that could be older than humans. It's at least as plausible an idea in Mage as humans being older than earth. But is it older than Avatars? Is it older than Pure Ones? Is it older than forces that can change reality? Were the rules ever concrete, or were they chosen by Will all the way down?<br /> <br /> And even if there is some arbitrary baseline set of rules, you're not saying how they keep the consensus from changing the shape of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This doesn't change the fact that human minds aren't responsible for shaping reality. We don't know which entity is older or created the WoD reality, but we know that weren't humans. The point is, Consensus have not the power to change universe laws, it just dictates what is easier to change usin will and what isn't (coincidetn/vulgar).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T20:59:54-07:00","id":968347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=968302#post968302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This doesn't change the fact that human minds aren't responsible for shaping reality. We don't know which entity is older or created the WoD reality, but we know that weren't humans. The point is, Consensus have not the power to change universe laws, it just dictates what is easier to change usin will and what isn't (coincidetn/vulgar).</div> </div> </div> </div>But human minds are responsible for reshaping reality. That's one of the principles of Mage. <br /> <br /> You are going to have to clarify here because you are either saying that the Consensus only changes how magic works, which is just flatly untrue, or you are only talking about a few key principles that can't be changed and in those cases the consensus determines how hard it is to magically override them. The second one might be true for some specific Cosmological Constants/Earthly Foundations, but the first one just isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T21:31:58-07:00","id":968356,"title":"","content":"The problem with that position, and many of the other subjective positions offered by a lot of Mage players, is that they are implicitly bigoted positions that justify oppression and genocide. I will explain. <br /> <br /> The Consensus before the 1960s said that women, non-whites, homosexuals, etc were genetically inferior to straight white men. If the Consensus shapes reality, then the position of society before the 1960s was correct and everyone was genetically inferior to straight white men. If the Consensus just shapes magic, then the position of society before the 1960s was incorrect and straight white men were just bigoted.<br /> <br /> The Consensus of the Old World before the 1400s said that there were no unknown continents, so the Americas were not thought to exist. If the Consensus shapes reality, then the Americas did not exist before the 1400s and the Americas were created to be conquered by European men and, by extension, the Native Americans were created to be the victims of European men. If the Consensus iust shapes magic, then the Americas existed before the 1400s and European men were just genocidal maniacs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T00:49:09-07:00","id":968403,"title":"","content":"You forget, that the Natives have also a word to say in that matter.<br /> In the past there where separate consensus bubbles akin to reality zones. Nowadays there is one big bubble with som zones and the occassional backwater sub-bubble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T04:52:12-07:00","id":968454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=968356#post968356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with that position, and many of the other subjective positions offered by a lot of Mage players, is that they are implicitly bigoted positions that justify oppression and genocide. I will explain.<br /> <br /> The Consensus before the 1960s said that women, non-whites, homosexuals, etc were genetically inferior to straight white men. If the Consensus shapes reality, then the position of society before the 1960s was correct and everyone was genetically inferior to straight white men. If the Consensus just shapes magic, then the position of society before the 1960s was incorrect and straight white men were just bigoted.<br /> <br /> The Consensus of the Old World before the 1400s said that there were no unknown continents, so the Americas were not thought to exist. If the Consensus shapes reality, then the Americas did not exist before the 1400s and the Americas were created to be conquered by European men and, by extension, the Native Americans were created to be the victims of European men. If the Consensus iust shapes magic, then the Americas existed before the 1400s and European men were just genocidal maniacs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with Nonsense on this one. Humans are humans and they have the same impact on the Consensus regardless of race, gender, preference, or creed. North Americans don't need Europeans to validate the existence of their continent any more than Europeans need North Americans to do likewise.<br /> <br /> By the same token the Consensus can't affect the impact of people on the Consensus. It can't make them stupid. It can't make them incapable of holding beliefs. It can't affect their minds or behavior. It can't make them disappear. It can't make them inferior. It is, by definition, made up of the collective belief of everybody in the region, not some more than others. At best it can create a physical or genetic difference (such an X vs a Y chromosome) but it can't say one is more important than the other. Everyone has the same impact on the Consensus.<br /> <br /> Edit: I have to expand on this, because it's really important to the entire idea of Mage. Mages have phenomenal cosmic power, they can make anything they can dream of happen, but they cannot make themselves <i>right</i>. Value judgements like right and wrong, superior and inferior, valuable and worthless are unprovable. Even if someone convinces everyone in the world that Freedom is better than Tyrrany or that Star Bellies are better than Plain, they still won't have a single thing to point to that says they are correct. Mages fight and kill and die for the ideals they believe in but no amount of magic or Consensus can force those ideas to be right or wrong. They just have to pick their sides and hope they aren't fooling themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 09-13-2016, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T06:09:49-07:00","id":968472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=968347#post968347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But human minds are responsible for reshaping reality. That's one of the principles of Mage. <br /> <br /> You are going to have to clarify here because you are either saying that the Consensus only changes how magic works, which is just flatly untrue, or you are only talking about a few key principles that can't be changed and in those cases the consensus determines how hard it is to magically override them. The second one might be true for some specific Cosmological Constants/Earthly Foundations, but the first one just isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Individual human minds can actively shape reality. Consensus onlybshape reality ny allowing reality to be shaped easier, not directly shaping it. The consensus don't change reality by itself, it's just a meter of how easily something can be done by magick. <br /> <br /> Also, consensus isn't opinion, it's belief that something exists or is possible. So, believing that it's possible to jump 10 meter straight makes it easier to jump 10 meter straight. Now, if a bunch of people think that grass are blue or the earth is flat won't make grass bluer or earth flatter, unless some crazy archmage pull a massive ritual to chamge grass color or earth shape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T06:15:05-07:00","id":968473,"title":"","content":"The problem with the position that the Consensus shapes reality is that the Consensus then does change people if it changes reality. The genetic and phenotype changes that you mention change people biologically and psychologically. Unless you are saying that human biology and human psychology have no impact on humans unless they believe so, you cannot take the position that the Consensus cannot impact people if it changes reality.<br /> <br /> Here is an example. Did cancer exist before it was quantified by the ancient Greeks? Did it only exist for the ancient Greeks and spread like a contagious disease as the idea of cancer spread throughout the world? Do people only get cancer because they believe in the existence of cancer? If the Consensus shapes reality, then cancer is a creation of belief and people only die of cancer because they (or society) believe in cancer. If the Consensus only shapes magic, then cancer is just a misfortune that may be cured with magic (or science).<br /> <br /> The same position can be taken with any disease. If the Consensus shapes reality, then people get diseases because they (or society) believe in the disease. If the Consensus only shapes magic, then diseases are misfortunes that can be cured by magic (or science).<br /> <br /> We can even get more applied than the example of diseases. Why do guns kill people? If the Consensus shapes reality, guns only kill people because the Consensus tells the attacker and the defender that guns are lethal. Since the historical record is pretty clear that guns killed people from cultures that had never previously encountered guns, you have evidence of the clash of two forms of Consensus. The European Consensus was stronger than the non-European Consensus in the case of guns (and diseases), allowing Europeans to commit genocide on non-Europeans. If the Consensus could not change people, then non-Europeans should have been immune to bullets (and also to the diseases that the Europeans brought). If the Consensus only shapes magic, however, then guns (and diseases) killed the non-Europeans due to physical laws rather than because the non-Europeans had an inferior Consensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T07:28:07-07:00","id":968507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=968473#post968473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with the position that the Consensus shapes reality is that the Consensus then does change people if it changes reality. The genetic and phenotype changes that you mention change people biologically and psychologically. Unless you are saying that human biology and human psychology have no impact on humans unless they believe so, you cannot take the position that the Consensus cannot impact people if it changes reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do, but keep in mind that those changes were made as alternate explanations for what people were already seen to be like. Men and women wouldn't undergo a massive change in personality the moment X and Y chromosomes were accepted because men and women already existed before that. At most you'd see a kind of slow change of dispositions in the sexes, but only as a generality, nothing that forces people to behave a certain way.<br /> <br /> What you wouldn't get is a sudden change that drastically and forcibly alters behaviors and opinions. There's an inertia to belief. Day to day life remains much the same even after a complete paradigm shift.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Here is an example. Did cancer exist before it was quantified by the ancient Greeks? Did it only exist for the ancient Greeks and spread like a contagious disease as the idea of cancer spread throughout the world? Do people only get cancer because they believe in the existence of cancer? If the Consensus shapes reality, then cancer is a creation of belief and people only die of cancer because they (or society) believe in cancer. If the Consensus only shapes magic, then cancer is just a misfortune that may be cured with magic (or science).<br /> <br /> The same position can be taken with any disease. If the Consensus shapes reality, then people get diseases because they (or society) believe in the disease. If the Consensus only shapes magic, then diseases are misfortunes that can be cured by magic (or science). </div> </div> </div>This isn't that hard to explain in a Consensual Reality. Cancer might not have existed before then but wasting diseases almost certainly did. There's no discontinuity, no &quot;one day there were no wasting diseases, then BAM! Cancer!&quot; What spread was not disease itself but a new idea of how disease worked. And yes, that new idea, and all the ideas that came after it gradually changed the way diseases did manifest and made certain symptoms possible or impossible. Gradually.<br /> <br /> And yes, it is entirely plausible that people only get sick because societies believe they get sick. It's a nasty consequence of the metaphysics of Mage, but there's nothing game breaking or theme breaking about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We can even get more applied than the example of diseases. Why do guns kill people? If the Consensus shapes reality, guns only kill people because the Consensus tells the attacker and the defender that guns are lethal. Since the historical record is pretty clear that guns killed people from cultures that had never previously encountered guns, you have evidence of the clash of two forms of Consensus. The European Consensus was stronger than the non-European Consensus in the case of guns (and diseases), allowing Europeans to commit genocide on non-Europeans. If the Consensus could not change people, then non-Europeans should have been immune to bullets (and also to the diseases that the Europeans brought). If the Consensus only shapes magic, however, then guns (and diseases) killed the non-Europeans due to physical laws rather than because the non-Europeans had an inferior Consensus. </div> </div> </div>Guns kill people because severe organ damage and blood loss kills people. This is something that was well known millennia before guns were ever invented. The Consensus changes involved with making guns possible involved convincing people that controlled explosions could semi-reliably make pieces of metal fly really quickly in a controlled way. That's why, when you take a gun into a different reality zone and it fails you generally get a gun that won't fire, not bullets that bounce off of people.<br /> <br /> Likewise most, if not all of the world's societies had an idea of plagues and disease and sometimes even a knowledge that newcomers bring disease. So they wouldn't have been paradigmatically resistant to European illness. Non European Consensuses weren't inferior, they just weren't resistant to the ideas Europeans were using to take over.<br /> <br /> ,And if we're honest, they didn't have the backing of a culturally imperialistic, monomaniacal cult of Mages that was sanitizing the world before the Traditions could even get their boots on. The Order of Reason played a big role in the advancement of the Western consensus.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T07:32:36-07:00","id":968508,"title":"","content":"Dude.... Consensus just makes magic easier or harder to do.<br /> It dictates if somethimg can happen or exist. It doesn't change reality directly. Our physics still exists and things get created or extinr normally. Consensus is just one of the variables that affect reality. You're saying as everything is a result of how consensus works.<br /> Cancers existed since it was mutated naturally, guns kill people,etc<br /> <br /> The kind of impact consensus can have directly in the world is making hard for things that aren't be\u00f1ieved or aren't possible to happen to happen/exist. Like, before it was easier to fly and there qere dragons, now not so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T08:19:55-07:00","id":968533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=968508#post968508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude.... Consensus just makes magic easier or harder to do.<br /> It dictates if somethimg can happen or exist. It doesn't change reality directly. Our physics still exists and things get created or extinr normally. Consensus is just one of the variables that affect reality. You're saying as everything is a result of how consensus works.<br /> Cancers existed since it was mutated naturally, guns kill people,etc<br /> <br /> The kind of impact consensus can have directly in the world is making hard for things that aren't be\u00f1ieved or aren't possible to happen to happen/exist. Like, before it was easier to fly and there qere dragons, now not so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's what I thought you were saying, and it is wrong. The Technocracy are not the discoverers of a one true physics. Modern physics, as we know it now did not work back when the Order of Reason was just getting going (1325). Electric circuits did not work until the consensus was convinced of them hundreds of years later. The consensus had to be convinced that batteries worked, they had to be convinced that nuclear explosions could happen. Those things couldn't happen until then. They weren't being suppressed by the consensus, the consensus didn't even know about them. They failed because no one believed in them.<br /> <br /> That is one of basic ideas of Mage, the Technocracy is not in the lead because they are right, but because they've been better at spreading their ideas to the masses. They're using the same 'magic' as everyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T08:26:45-07:00","id":968537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=968533#post968533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that's what I thought you were saying, and it is wrong. The Technocracy are not the discoverers of a one true physics. Modern physics, as we know it now did not work back when the Order of Reason was just getting going (1325). Electric circuits did not work until the consensus was convinced of them hundreds of years later. The consensus had to be convinced that batteries worked, they had to be convinced that nuclear explosions could happen. Those things couldn't happen until then. They weren't being suppressed by the consensus, the consensus didn't even know about them. They failed because no one believed in them.<br /> <br /> That is one of basic ideas of Mage, the Technocracy is not in the lead because they are right, but because they've been better at spreading their ideas to the masses. They're using the same 'magic' as everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything that didn't worked before because of the consensus was just vulgar. It doesn't mean the consensus created them later nor that consensus is capable of make fundamentals chamges like the earyh being flat.<br /> <br /> One thing is allowing things to exist/happen easily, another is dictating how thimgs really are. No, the earth wasn't flat back then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T09:04:08-07:00","id":968552,"title":"","content":"The problem with the Consensus, and everything in Mage practically, is that they are internally inconsistent. Either reality is shaped by the Consensus or only magic is shaped by the Consensus. Of course, the Consensus is really just an excuse for the internally inconsistent and poorly written game mechanics that have been the hallmark of Mage for the last 20 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T09:06:08-07:00","id":968553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=968537#post968537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everything that didn't worked before because of the consensus was just vulgar. It doesn't mean the consensus created them later nor that consensus is capable of make fundamentals chamges like the earyh being flat.<br /> <br /> One thing is allowing things to exist/happen easily, another is dictating how thimgs really are. No, the earth wasn't flat back then.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does actually mean that. There is no reason whatsoever to think that modern science occupies some kind of special place in Mage, that it alone is right, that bodies always had cells, that atoms always had electrons and nuclei, and that for some reason the consensus has just been suppressing that until now. There is no reason to think that the Technocracy has just lucked out and every major paradigm they've pushed has happened to be the way things really are.<br /> <br /> I realize that the earth once being flat is counter-intuitive, and I see why you want to reject it. And if it is that important to you, feel free to make that one of the Earthly Foundations (just because I avoid using them doesn't mean you have to). A flat earth does not, however, violate the themes or metaphysics of Mage. A one true physics does.<br /> <br /> And by the way, there's an even stranger form the Earth might have taken in the past. I just need to check one thing first. Does anyone remember if all the mapping and exploring the Explorators were doing in the early days of the Order of Reason was actually locking geography into place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T10:55:56-07:00","id":968619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=968553#post968553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does actually mean that. There is no reason whatsoever to think that modern science occupies some kind of special place in Mage, that it alone is right, that bodies always had cells, that atoms always had electrons and nuclei, and that for some reason the consensus has just been suppressing that until now. There is no reason to think that the Technocracy has just lucked out and every major paradigm they've pushed has happened to be the way things really are.<br /> <br /> I realize that the earth once being flat is counter-intuitive, and I see why you want to reject it. And if it is that important to you, feel free to make that one of the Earthly Foundations (just because I avoid using them doesn't mean you have to). A flat earth does not, however, violate the themes or metaphysics of Mage. A one true physics does.<br /> <br /> And by the way, there's an even stranger form the Earth might have taken in the past. I just need to check one thing first. Does anyone remember if all the mapping and exploring the Explorators were doing in the early days of the Order of Reason was actually locking geography into place?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there is a Reality and it have its own rules. The Technocracy didn't invented them, they just try to make them stricter.<br /> Unless there is some statement that says that the earth were flat or anything umlike our real world it isn't. Remember thw WoD is pretty similar to our real world, except for some differences.<br /> <br /> Modern science just study the universe how it really is, but it doesnt consider the mutability of reality thanks to Technocracy. <br /> <br /> I think there is no evidence for both our points, i just feel the burden of proving is yours. To me Mage Reality is exactly like ours, except for what they say it isn't. Also it makes more sense too. Consensus isn't an effect, black people won't get intellectually inferior because a bunch of racists think so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:12:52-07:00","id":968627,"title":"","content":"I am always confused by the &quot;just because everyone believes grass is blue/the sky is green doesn't mean that it becomes so&quot; example in these debates because, uh, if we all decided that grass was blue then it'd be blue, in the real world, without any fancy consensual reality mojo. It's not like the arbitrary labels on how one defines colors were a divine revelation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:24:56-07:00","id":968635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=968454#post968454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the same token the Consensus can't affect the impact of people on the Consensus. It can't make them stupid. It can't make them incapable of holding beliefs. It can't affect their minds or behavior. It can't make them disappear. It can't make them inferior. It is, by definition, made up of the collective belief of everybody in the region, not some more than others. At best it can create a physical or genetic difference (such an X vs a Y chromosome) but it can't say one is more important than the other. Everyone has the same impact on the Consensus.<br /> <br /> Edit: I have to expand on this, because it's really important to the entire idea of Mage. Mages have phenomenal cosmic power, they can make anything they can dream of happen, but they cannot make themselves <i>right</i>. Value judgements like right and wrong, superior and inferior, valuable and worthless are unprovable. Even if someone convinces everyone in the world that Freedom is better than Tyrrany or that Star Bellies are better than Plain, they still won't have a single thing to point to that says they are correct. Mages fight and kill and die for the ideals they believe in but no amount of magic or Consensus can force those ideas to be right or wrong. They just have to pick their sides and hope they aren't fooling themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm. I'm not so sure about your claim that the Consensus can't affect intelligence. Intelligence, after all, doesn't substantively affect the ability to <i>have</i> beliefs; it might affect what conclusions someone reaches, but so can Conditioning and other Mind effects.<br /> <br /> Essentially, while I'm fine with saying &quot;Consensus can't affect Avatars, which are the source of Consensus&quot;, I'm not with saying &quot;the Consensus can't influence minds at all, apart from specifics like language and so on&quot;. If that makes sense.<br /> <br /> Also, it seems... fitting?... to me that the metaphor for societal pressures can materially disadvantage oppressed minority factions. It's an allegory for the effects of poverty and discrimination on education and opportunities and identity.<br /> <br /> It's utterly horrible too! And since we're playing World of Darkness, that's a good thing. Fighting to influence the beliefs of the Sleepers is a core part of Mage, after all.<br /> <br /> (Mages, Sorcerers, and other protagonisty sorts can of course defy these limitations as individuals, though the Consensus may well backlash on them for it...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:26:03-07:00","id":968637,"title":"","content":"Ages past a technomancer could use a Forces/Prime effect channeled through a tube like object. It was vain magick(the name for vulgar magick at the time)<br /> <br /> Nowadays you do not need Forces to shoot metal. You only need a tube like object. Because Consensus says so. It is not magick anymore.<br /> <br /> I suggest reading Mage the Sorcerers Crusade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T12:28:47-07:00","id":968679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=968619#post968619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well there is a Reality and it have its own rules. The Technocracy didn't invented them, they just try to make them stricter.<br /> Unless there is some statement that says that the earth were flat or anything umlike our real world it isn't. Remember thw WoD is pretty similar to our real world, except for some differences.<br /> <br /> Modern science just study the universe how it really is, but it doesnt consider the mutability of reality thanks to Technocracy.<br /> <br /> I think there is no evidence for both our points, i just feel the burden of proving is yours. To me Mage Reality is exactly like ours, except for what they say it isn't. Also it makes more sense too. Consensus isn't an effect, black people won't get intellectually inferior because a bunch of racists think so...</div> </div> </div> </div>1) I already covered how the Consensus can't make anyone intellectually inferior already. It doesn't work. The consensus can't undercut itself. If, for whatever reason, that doesn't cut it for you, you can either roll with it (as Quantumboost said, horrible consequences are in theme for WoD games) or house rule it away, What you can't do is insist that one of the core ideas of Mage must not be one of the core ideas of Mage.<br /> <br /> 2) The world is pretty similar to ours <i>right now</i>, and that is explicitly because the Technocracy has been working hard to bring about the modern views of science, economics, medicine, etc. <br /> <br /> 3) My view- that reality is determined by belief and that it was substantially different in previous eras- is backed up by the books. You can cede that you have no evidence for your points if you want, but...<br /> <br /> 4) I don't accept &quot;I don't have to prove my case but you have to prove yours&quot; at the best of times, but especially not in Mage, an Epic Game of Reality on the Brink. You are making some serious claims here, ones that run directly against Mage as written. You have to back them up.<br /> <br /> That said since I did say both sides carry a burden of proof, I'll pull a few lines from M20. M2nd or MRev would give even stronger examples because M20 is written in a subjective voice, but I don't have those with me right now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20 Page 48</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who makes that ocean? That debate\u2019s been going for ages. As best as we can figure, though, the mass of our Earth\u2019s reality comes from those supposed Sleepers and the combined force of their belief.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20 Page 62</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reality has rules, and those rules are decided by the Consensus: the collective power of belief across the world. The term began as a Technocratic buzzword, but plenty of other mages use it too. Consensual reality is essentially the established baseline reality for our Earth. It\u2019s got a certain amount of give to it, but many laws are immutable. That which goes up must come down. An object in motion tends to stay in motion. An object at rest tends to stay at rest.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20 Page 63</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> for now at least, a scientific belief system holds the most favorable edge in the Consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>So most of reality, including the parts we are most tempted to consider fixed are determined by the consensus. In fact that line &quot;Consensual reality is essentially the baseline reality for our Earth&quot; is particularly important because baseline reality is a term used to define Earthly Foundations. Indeed, rereading the section on Earthly Foundations, I see nothing saying they aren't also products of the Consensus.<br /> <br /> I'm certainly willing to conceded that Mage has, in the past, called out a few specific, hard to ST cases as being outside the realm of the Consensus to affect. The majority of reality, though, is explicitly defined by belief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T14:54:31-07:00","id":968755,"title":"","content":"Obviously I'm no great scholar of Mage, it's rules, or it's dogma... but I'm under the impression that the Consensus well agrees that people can't summon a demon, incinerate its flesh with lightning bolts from their fingertips, shapeshift into a bull and stomp the demon skull into powder, all just so they can use it as an ingredient for a sack of sparkly dust that makes people horny (literally) when you blow it in their face... but each and every one of those things is possible, paradox-free, through Hedgemagic. Just as Werewolves and Vampires and Mummies and countless umbral planes and their spirit denizens all exist... but paradox doesn't touch them because they're part of &quot;the establishment&quot;, as it were.<br /> <br /> I feel like that much alone implies there are rules to the universe that pre-date or overpower the consensus of puny humans... unless you chose to write that off as an anti-thematic concession that had to be made for Mage to be in the WoD and not a standalone game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T17:08:55-07:00","id":968837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=968679#post968679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So most of reality, including the parts we are most tempted to consider fixed are determined by the consensus. In fact that line &quot;Consensual reality is essentially the baseline reality for our Earth&quot; is particularly important because baseline reality is a term used to define Earthly Foundations. Indeed, rereading the section on Earthly Foundations, I see nothing saying they aren't also products of the Consensus.<br /> <br /> I'm certainly willing to conceded that Mage has, in the past, called out a few specific, hard to ST cases as being outside the realm of the Consensus to affect. The majority of reality, though, is explicitly defined by belief.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nowhere in your quotes it is said that consensus have the power of changing that magick do. That's what you're saying that consensus can shape reality directly like an Effect, which isn't true. All consensus can do is determine what is acceptable to do by the reality itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Originally posted by <b>M20 Page 48</b></i><br /> <i>Who makes that ocean? That debate\u2019s been going for ages. As best as we can figure, though, the mass of our Earth\u2019s reality comes from those supposed Sleepers and the combined force of their belief.</i> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Nothing new here. We all know consensus is a result of all the sleepers minds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Originally posted by <b>M20 Page 62</b></i><br /> <i>Reality has rules, and those rules are decided by the Consensus: the collective power of belief across the world. The term began as a Technocratic buzzword, but plenty of other mages use it too. Consensual reality is essentially the established baseline reality for our Earth. It\u2019s got a certain amount of give to it, but many laws are immutable. That which goes up must come down. An object in motion tends to stay in motion. An object at rest tends to stay at rest.</i> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That's exactly what I was saying. Consensus can set some rules, but it is not an active change in reality other than making change itself possible or no. Consensus is not a mage casting effects. Also, this quote says that some changes cannot ever be accepted even if Consensus try it. This means Consensus isn't even a definitive set of rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Originally posted by <b>M20 Page 63</b></i><br /> <i>for now at least, a scientific belief system holds the most favorable edge in the Consensus.</i> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Again, nothing new. We all know that Consensus tends to let scientifically based effects go as coincidental because of all the Technocrat propaganda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T18:29:04-07:00","id":968890,"title":"","content":"It lets Technocracy magic be coincidental. Science is not magic, it is the manifestation of the will of the Weaver (Book of the Weaver (Revised), p. 41). Oh, and it is the Weaver, not the Consensus, that decides what magic is coincidental or vulgar. The Technocracy just gets the benefit of the doubt from Her because they are working for the same goals. Whether or not human beings believe in nanotech will not make nanotech science, it is whether or not the Weaver decides that nanotech is beneficial to Her goals that makes it science.<br /> <br /> That is the problem of the entire argument. We have creatures within the same Universe that predate humans by hundreds of millions of years and spiritual entities that predate humans by billion of years, so the idea that human belief shapes anything is just the delusions of Mages. There entire Avatar War is meaningless because it is the Weaver that determines whether magic is coincidental or not, not Mages or Sleepers, and all that Mages can do is attempt either to weaken the Weaver or the strengthen the Weaver. The Technocracy just caught earlier than the other Mages and have convinced the Weaver to shape Her interpretation of Reality to fit within their paradigms instead of the paradigms of other Mages. If the Technocracy stopped being useful to the Weaver, its Mages would soon find that their magic would be vulgar as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T19:38:32-07:00","id":968933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=968837#post968837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing new here. We all know consensus is a result of all the sleepers minds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read it again, Revan. &quot;The mass of our Earth's <b>reality</b> comes from those supposed sleepers and the <b>combined force of their belief</b>&quot; The quote doesn't just define what the consensus is, it also says what effect it has: it is making reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's exactly what I was saying. Consensus can set some rules, but it is not an active change in reality other than making change itself possible or no. Consensus is not a mage casting effects. Also, this quote says that some changes cannot ever be accepted even if Consensus try it. This means Consensus isn't even a definitive set of rules. </div> </div> </div>Read it again, Revan. &quot;Consensual reality is essentially the established baseline reality for our Earth.&quot; Those immutable laws came from consensus not a set of one true physics. Far from saying the consensus can't change them, this quote says that it made them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, nothing new. We all know that Consensus tends to let scientifically based effects go as coincidental because of all the Technocrat propaganda. </div> </div> </div>Read it again, Rev- Actually I get why this one seems unimpressive. The 'for now' is important. In the light of the other two quotes this one shows that the consensus does change reality, specifically, it shows that the rules of reality have not always been this way. Not just what is coincidental or believable, the actual rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=968837#post968837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nowhere in your quotes it is said that consensus have the power of changing that magick do. That's what you're saying that consensus can shape reality directly like an Effect, which isn't true. All consensus can do is determine what is acceptable to do by the reality itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that's exactly what the quotes show. Repeatedly. The mass of reality comes from belief. The rules are made by the consensus. Belief shapes the world, it changes what the world <i>is</i>.<br /> <br /> And just to show that this is not just taking M20 out of context.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage 2nd Edition, Page 61 (the emphasis was in the book)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This metaphysical premise holds that we play a far more active role in the universal pageant than sleeper philosophy would have us believe. We, as conscious beings, <b>are</b> the cause, and the universe, or the boundaries of it, is <b>our</b> effect.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage 2nd Edition, Page 61</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Material reality is a consensual hallucination which the vast majority of humanity agrees upon.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the record, M2nd presents these as how mages see the metaphysics of their world, but it is also presented as the actual metaphysics of magic. <br /> <br /> Also on the same page is talk of gravity and the atmosphere being harder to manipulate, and once again, this is attributed to the consensus. Some mages are said to speculate that these specific elements might predate the Pure Ones, and even then that is mostly an explanation for why they are so deeply ingrained in the <i>consensus</i>.<br /> <br /> There are other references in the book to widespread beliefs becoming part of static reality and mundane technology breaking down in the remote areas of the world, but I'm done quoting. Belief changes reality. Change the consensus, change reality. The Technocracy has done this successfully.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Now, I've provided quotes. You made a claim that modern physics is, in fact, the baseline reality and the consensus just says what kind of magic can override it easily. It's time for you to back that up with something concrete.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T20:14:25-07:00","id":968955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=968755#post968755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously I'm no great scholar of Mage, it's rules, or it's dogma... but I'm under the impression that the Consensus well agrees that people can't summon a demon, incinerate its flesh with lightning bolts from their fingertips, shapeshift into a bull and stomp the demon skull into powder, all just so they can use it as an ingredient for a sack of sparkly dust that makes people horny (literally) when you blow it in their face... but each and every one of those things is possible, paradox-free, through Hedgemagic. Just as Werewolves and Vampires and Mummies and countless umbral planes and their spirit denizens all exist... but paradox doesn't touch them because they're part of &quot;the establishment&quot;, as it were.<br /> <br /> I feel like that much alone implies there are rules to the universe that pre-date or overpower the consensus of puny humans... unless you chose to write that off as an anti-thematic concession that had to be made for Mage to be in the WoD and not a standalone game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hedge magic is specifically covered in Mage, though, it works by conforming to mythic threads and other residual beliefs that remain in the collective unconscious. <br /> <br /> As for the other supernaturals, you got it exactly. The original game lines of the classic World of Darkness were not written with crossovers in mind and they stomp all over eachother's core ideas. In Mage the other supernaturals are usually attributed to Mythic Threads or Cosmological Constants, but it is admittedly a very clunky patch.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=968890#post968890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It lets Technocracy magic be coincidental. Science is not magic, it is the manifestation of the will of the Weaver (Book of the Weaver (Revised), p. 41). Oh, and it is the Weaver, not the Consensus, that decides what magic is coincidental or vulgar. The Technocracy just gets the benefit of the doubt from Her because they are working for the same goals. Whether or not human beings believe in nanotech will not make nanotech science, it is whether or not the Weaver decides that nanotech is beneficial to Her goals that makes it science.</div> </div> </div> </div>Book of the Weaver is a WtA book, not a Mage one. Unless it is being used for a crossover, it is not reasonable to use a Werewolf supplement to override the Mage <i>corebooks'</i> explanation of how Magic works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T21:35:12-07:00","id":969002,"title":"","content":"It is explicitly a crossover book because it is also a Technocracy book (it gives rules on Technomancer Devices, WeaverTech, and relations between Technocratic Mages and Weaver Spirits). Anyway, the Mage books are mostly written from the Mage perspective, which means they are written from the perspective of a bunch of sociopathic narcissists who combine borderline personality disorder with a god complex, and they are the sane Mages. I think that I will trust the relatively objective, if biased and distorted, Werewolf books over the utterly insanely subjective Mage books whenever possible (the Book of Madness being a notable exception).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T23:33:13-07:00","id":969042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=969002#post969002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is explicitly a crossover book because it is also a Technocracy book (it gives rules on Technomancer Devices, WeaverTech, and relations between Technocratic Mages and Weaver Spirits).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a WtA book (as prominently stated on the cover and back), with ideas and rules for adding the Technocracy splats <i>to a WtA game,</i> as seen on page 89. Somebody going for the literal crossover books that mention being for 'X and Mage' or 'Mage and X' on front/back will never hold this book in their hands.<br /> <br /> It's not a neutral crossover book that is meant to be added to a Mage game in turn. It's meant for WtA games.<br /> <br /> Now, of course there are probably a few ST that *are* trying to run a completely neutral crossover where both gamelines' lores and origin stories are as valid as possible.. Then the Vampire ST comes in and says 'Nah, God made it all, see this and that.' and the mess is complete.<br /> OWoD doesn't work for neutral crossovers. The ST needs to decide what gameline to run primarily, lore/origin-wise, and add the other gamelines' splats to.<br /> <br /> P.s.<br /> Which is why I'm really..intrigued to see how they want to handle the One World of Darkness unification of the settings. If it actually will be that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-14-2016, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T01:19:59-07:00","id":969086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=968890#post968890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Technocracy just caught earlier than the other Mages and have convinced the Weaver to shape Her interpretation of Reality to fit within their paradigms instead of the paradigms of other Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>This assumption makes the NWO Procedure &quot;Create Drone&quot; much more creepy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T03:27:12-07:00","id":969119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=968755#post968755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously I'm no great scholar of Mage, it's rules, or it's dogma... but I'm under the impression that the Consensus well agrees that people can't summon a demon, incinerate its flesh with lightning bolts from their fingertips, shapeshift into a bull and stomp the demon skull into powder, all just so they can use it as an ingredient for a sack of sparkly dust that makes people horny (literally) when you blow it in their face... but each and every one of those things is possible, paradox-free, through Hedgemagic. Just as Werewolves and Vampires and Mummies and countless umbral planes and their spirit denizens all exist... but paradox doesn't touch them because they're part of &quot;the establishment&quot;, as it were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, they are part of &quot;The establishment&quot;.<br /> <br /> In Mage, the rules that allow such beings to exist are called the &quot;Mythic Threads&quot; of reality, kind of the third part of the triad that makes up &quot;Consensus - Earthly Foundations - Mythic Threads&quot;.<br /> <br /> And as stated in some posts here, all of it is somewhat mallable by each other - but it's hard to do so, and is the topic of lots of debates.<br /> <br /> Some Mage players see the Vampire's dependance on blood and their weakness against sunlight as their form of 'paradox'. Likewise with the Shifter's sensitivity to certain materials (Silver/Gold/etc. depending on breed). This is just interpreation, and not something specifically stated by any books.<br /> <br /> But yes - ultimately all those things, the other supernatural splats as well as hedge magic and other numina - are part of reality, not working outside of it. It's a part of reality that the Consensus has not managed to force out - unlike the other Bygones, like dragons, fae, etc. etc. Those *were* forced to leave the Earth Realm by the Consensus.<br /> So, not only can the Consensus have an effect on Earthly Foundations to a small degree, it can have a bigger impact on the Mythic Threads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-14-2016, 06:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T15:03:39-07:00","id":969479,"title":"","content":"Do note that at least as of Revised, Hedge Magic does actually have what amounts to a Paradox Backlash for a Mage: it <i>fails outright</i> when there's active disbelief headed its way. Which is presumably how it manages to fit within the nature of reality, even when it seems to sort-of violate Consensus; when it doesn't fail, there's <i>just enough</i> give that the very restrained Avatar/Genius/thingy-which-makes-the-magic-go-do can sneak it in, but when there isn't it just goes &quot;nope&quot;.<br /> <br /> (This is at least moderately a concern with Hedge Magic because the person using it is usually metaphysically a human, just like Mages are)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-14-2016, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T19:03:04-07:00","id":969597,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> , you are using a quote from the book that clearly shows a in-game mage giving his thougths about the subject. The authors did that on purpose to let some primordial decision up to the ST, just like they don't specify how the univers/reality was created. Also, none of your quotes tells how much influence consensus can have on reality and it's probably left for the ST.<br /> <br /> By saying that Consensus makes reality, you're implying that there wasn't reality before the Consensus. And we know that human beings showed up on earth in the last few years of universe creation.<br /> <br /> You still have no evidence that reality is created by consensus itself. There were already a LOT of laws, basically every laws of physics before consensus showed up from the mind of human society.<br /> <br /> I think we both agree that reality isn't created by consensus, but molded by it. What we disagree is the level of influence it can have upon reality. According to you, almost anything can be changed/created by consensus.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter how much people believe that earth is 6000 years old, it just isn't. Consensus can't do shit about this. If suddenly 51% of world population start believeing the earth is flat won't change the shape of the planet. Such a violent change would extinguish all life in the planet. <br /> What if 51% of people believe that human beings are invisible? Do everyone on earth become invisible?<br /> <br /> The consensus analogy shows reality as a river and the mage is can swim in the same direction of the current (coincident) or against it (vulgar). The river can't swim itself, just as it cannot cast effects by itself. All it can do is let people swim easier or harder on what they want to do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, I've provided quotes. You made a claim that modern physics is, in fact, the baseline reality and the consensus just says what kind of magic can override it easily. It's time for you to back that up with something concrete. </div> </div> </div>All you provided was quotes from a &quot;mage&quot; telling that consensus is part of the reality. It doesn't say how much of reality it can change. You just interpreted that reality is a consequence of consensus, but we both know reality is older than consensus. As I read your quotes, there is nothing contradictory from the way I see things.<br /> <br /> About modern physics,the books never said that the basics laws of physics (gravity,earth shape, etc.) were different before human race, so there is no reason to think otherwise. Of course, after the consensus came in, lots of laws could be broken more easily by mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T22:06:14-07:00","id":969663,"title":"","content":"First off, Revan. If you aren't going to provide any quotes to back up your premise- specifically to back up the idea that modern physics is the original, fundamental, default reality of Mage- just tell me now. Because you are making an amazingly strong claim and thus far I haven't seen you provide any proof. I'm not going to continue arguing with you how &quot;consensual reality is the established baseline reality of our world&quot; means that consensual reality is the baseline reality of our world if you aren't going to act in good faith.<br /> <br /> On that note:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=969597#post969597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If suddenly 51% of world population start believeing the earth is flat won't change the shape of the planet. <b>Such a violent change would extinguish all life in the planet.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Do you even bother to read other people's arguments? Where did I ever say that the earth slowly and visibly wrapped itself from a flat island into a sphere? You are the one saying that. You are the only one saying that consensus shifts would have to be violent.<br /> <br /> The sleepers don't think the world is changing and they don't think that they are changing the world. They're just accepting a more convincing explanation for why life is the way it already is. So the world changes from flat to round and no one notices because on a local level nothing seems different. There's no violent upheaval because none is expected. From the outside things look dramatically different, but on the ground where everyone lives everything looks the same. The sleepers aren't even aware they've swapped one reality for another.<br /> <br /> And that's the key. Things like the shape of the earth, the way life works, the nature of matter, those are the easy things for the consensus to change, because all of the major differences are only visible from a perspective regular sleepers can't perceive. Whether bodies are swimming in the four humours or made up of billions of cells, they look the same to a regular person. Whether matter is made from the four classical elements or from the modern elements they look the same to a regular person.<br /> <br /> That's also why your invisibility complaint isn't an issue. The consensus quite likely could make everyone invisible, but you aren't going to convince 51% of the population that people are invisible. Not without blinding them first. Otherwise, they can already see that they aren't invisible. Like with gravity and the atmosphere, light and vision are something that most people interact with every day. Convincing them to ignore the expectations built over a lifetime is hard.<br /> <br /> Now do you see why your One True Physics idea isn't necessary, how there are at least some actual changes that could be made without destroying everything? And if not, will you offer at least some proof that the One True Physics is more than just your house rule?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T01:34:42-07:00","id":969754,"title":"","content":"The best proof of an underlying greater reality is the superiority of Sorcerers when it comes to countering the True Magick of Mages. Mechanically, a properly designed beginning Sorcerer can, without too much abuse of the system, remove four successes from any working of True Magick per turn (even more if they spend Mana or Willpower). Even if you ignore that, True Magick is incapable of functioning in the Deep Dreaming (which suggests a more fundamental physics than the physics of True Magick) and the superiority of elder vampires (which suggest that their capabilities are more fundamental than that of Mages). And you add the fact that every supernatural creature is immune to Paradox when they are using their powers, which suggests that they are, once again, operating on a more fundamental level than Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T01:49:12-07:00","id":969765,"title":"","content":"No one can prove that the world was not created last thursday. Likewise it is impossible to say how reality was before there was a consensus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T01:49:42-07:00","id":969766,"title":"","content":"No one can prove that the world was not created last thursday. Likewise it is impossible to prove how reality was before there was a consensus","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T07:32:39-07:00","id":969887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=969663#post969663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, Revan. If you aren't going to provide any quotes to back up your premise- specifically to back up the idea that modern physics is the original, fundamental, default reality of Mage- just tell me now. Because you are making an amazingly strong claim and thus far I haven't seen you provide any proof. I'm not going to continue arguing with you how &amp;quot;consensual reality is the established baseline reality of our world&amp;quot; means that consensual reality is the baseline reality of our world if you aren't going to act in good faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sigh.... If you really don't want to use logic and want some quote, as if the authors of this system gave everything to us, I'll quote the obvious lines that says the wod is like our own.<br /> <br /> From mage rev.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Mage: The Ascension, that same world exists. It has all the modern conveniences, historical foibles and raging debates. However, it's a darkened mirror of our universe (...). </div> </div> </div>And <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although the world of mages seems like our own, (...) </div> </div> </div>So, unless when stated otherwise, the WoD is just like our universe, which means the planet is round, there is a Force of gravity and everything else. Of course, ST is free to make it different in their own games, but don't show up in the forums telling that the earth was flat before people think it wasn't as if stated in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=969663#post969663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that note:<br /> <br /> Do you even bother to read other people's arguments? Where did I ever say that the earth slowly and visibly wrapped itself from a flat island into a sphere? You are the one saying that. You are the only one saying that consensus shifts would have to be violent.<br /> <br /> The sleepers don't think the world is changing and they don't think that they are changing the world. They're just accepting a more convincing explanation for why life is the way it already is. So the world changes from flat to round and no one notices because on a local level nothing seems different. There's no violent upheaval because none is expected. From the outside things look dramatically different, but on the ground where everyone lives everything looks the same. The sleepers aren't even aware they've swapped one reality for another.</div> </div> </div> </div>This implies that there is no law of physics outside what people believes. Like, people have to believe that a change on the shape of the earth would fuck up with the entire balance of the planet to the change really fuck it.<br /> It's the old &quot;if a tree falls down but there is no one to hear, does it make a sound?&quot; If that was the case nothing that people don't believe or know would exist or happen, which isn't the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=969663#post969663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's the key. Things like the shape of the earth, the way life works, the nature of matter, those are the easy things for the consensus to change, because all of the major differences are only visible from a perspective regular sleepers can't perceive. Whether bodies are swimming in the four humours or made up of billions of cells, they look the same to a regular person. Whether matter is made from the four classical elements or from the modern elements they look the same to a regular person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same as above. Also, there is no way we can tell if matter is made of atoms or the classic elements.This is clearly left open by the book. But the logical thinking would be mirroring our own world. As i quoted before, WoD is a mirror of our own. Again, you can make it different as a ST, but the default is the one we have here. That also makes things easier in game play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=969663#post969663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now do you see why your One True Physics idea isn't necessary, how there are at least some actual changes that could be made without destroying everything? And if not, will you offer at least some proof that the One True Physics is more than just your house rule?</div> </div> </div> </div>I provided. Actually, I would say that tjere is mo right answer, it's a ST call. But I guarantee that the majority of ST makes the WoD just like our own, simply because it's the default and easier to display. Just don't post things like &quot;the earth was flat before people believed it was round&quot; because that is a house rule..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T07:34:54-07:00","id":969888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=969766#post969766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one can prove that the world was not created last thursday. Likewise it is impossible to prove how reality was before there was a consensus</div> </div> </div> </div>Wtf? I was in the planwt last thursday and the planet too. By logic, this meams that the planet was created before. Please, start using logic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T07:48:51-07:00","id":969900,"title":"","content":"It is a common logical fallacy often associated with Creation myths. The idea being that an entity so powerful and detail oriented to be able to create your memories along with everything else. It is one of the reasons why Creation myths come with specific beginnings, to prevent people from descending into madness by questioning the validity of their own existence. <br /> <br /> It is also a common argument that people who believe in the intellectual infancy of solipsism retreat to (the 'you only exist because I believe that you exist' line of thinking). At best, it is used as the retreat of people who think they are philosophers but have not really bothered to spend time thinking about philosophy. At worst, it is the argument of sociopaths and psychopaths who lack the ability to come up with something creative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:20:44-07:00","id":969976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=969887#post969887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sigh.... If you really don't want to use logic and want some quote, as if the authors of this system gave everything to us, I'll quote the obvious lines that says the wod is like our own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Logic only works if your premises are valid. You are adding assumptions. You are then using those assumptions to prove themselves. That's circular reasoning. I'm asking you to back those claims. Speaking of which, your quotes don't. You claimed that the rules of Mage reality <i>have always been the same</i>, but you only provided information on what they are <i>right now</i>. What they are right now is not in question. You need to show where it says that they always were what they are right now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This implies that there is no law of physics outside what people believes. Like, people have to believe that a change on the shape of the earth would fuck up with the entire balance of the planet to the change really fuck it. </div> </div> </div>Yes, you're getting it now. That's exactly what it implies. You've been assuming a consistent set of physics. Mage never makes that claim.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's the old &quot;if a tree falls down but there is no one to hear, does it make a sound?&quot; If that was the case nothing that people don't believe or know would exist or happen, which isn't the case. </div> </div> </div>Well, yes. Hence why a lot of technology stops working in the remote regions of the world. The principles it operates on are not known there and so things like electric circuits don't work.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Same as above. Also, there is no way we can tell if matter is made of atoms or the classic elements.This is clearly left open by the book. But the logical thinking would be mirroring our own world. As i quoted before, WoD is a mirror of our own. </div> </div> </div>Again, it's a mirror of our own, for right now. Right now WoD matter could very well be made of atoms. The question is what was it before modern atomic theory was accepted by the masses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I provided. Actually, I would say that tjere is mo right answer, it's a ST call. But I guarantee that the majority of ST makes the WoD just like our own, simply because it's the default and easier to display. Just don't post things like &quot;the earth was flat before people believed it was round&quot; because that is a house rule. </div> </div> </div>Is this some sort of olive branch? You'll admit you are using house rules if I do? Sorry, but since you haven't provided any indication that your One True Physics is the default, and indeed several times you've indicated that you can't, it doesn't work. Consensual reality is explicitly stated in the books, a One True Physics is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 09-15-2016, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T12:04:06-07:00","id":970086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=969976#post969976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Logic only works if your premises are valid. You are adding assumptions. You are then using those assumptions to prove themselves. That's circular reasoning. I'm asking you to back those claims. Speaking of which, your quotes don't. You claimed that the rules of Mage reality <i>have always been the same</i>, but you only provided information on what they are <i>right now</i>. What they are right now is not in question. You need to show where it says that they always were what they are right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Show me that before consensus reality wasn't a sponge bob show and earth hadn't the shape of a car. Just like we can't exactly prove this in real life, there is absolutely no evidence to back this up. The burden of proof belongs to whom claim those things.<br /> <br /> All you could show is that consensus is a fundamental part of reality, which i nwver disagreed. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=969976#post969976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, you're getting it now. That's exactly what it implies. You've been assuming a consistent set of physics. Mage never makes that claim.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does. When you consider that tje wod is similar to ours. Hell, even a D&amp;D universe follow the premises of our physics. If some claim must be made is that it is different, and Mage only claims this when dealing with magick and consensus.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=969976#post969976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yes. Hence why a lot of technology stops working in the remote regions of the world. The principles it operates on are not known there and so things like electric circuits don't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technology doesn't work on those regions because consensus there makes it hard, just like the swiming against the river analogy. This has nothing to do with consensus actively changing reality itself, it's just making it harder for someone to make the change. There must be a &quot;mage&quot; trying to change the reality by using the technology. This example doesn't help your cause.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=969976#post969976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, it's a mirror of our own, for right now. Right now WoD matter could very well be made of atoms. The question is what was it before modern atomic theory was accepted by the masses.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was probably made of atoms, thiugh it was harder for mages to make effects that dealt with atoms, since consensus didn't know about them. That's what consensus do, it make things harder to do, not actively change how things are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=969976#post969976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this some sort of olive branch? You'll admit you are using house rules if I do? Sorry, but since you haven't provided any indication that your One True Physics is the default, and indeed several times you've indicated that you can't, it doesn't work. Consensual reality is explicitly stated in the books, a One True Physics is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't deny consensus reality, it is clearly stated in the books. What I disagree is how it affect the universe. Which you also can't prove that it has this kind of power over the reality that you are saying. No one True Physics either, just the earthly foundations that can't be changed. Of course that are aspects of physics that can be changed, but the only change that can be made by consensus is making it more possible. Actively changes needs mages","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 09-15-2016, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T12:24:05-07:00","id":970104,"title":"","content":"But werewolves (and fomori) are able to use satellite cell phones in the Amazon, so how does that work with the consensus negatively influencing technology? In addition, satellites work in GEO, which is tens of thousands of miles away from the nearest human being, so how does the consensus effect things that far out (much less the probes that have exited the Sol System)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T12:56:37-07:00","id":970125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=970086#post970086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Show me that before consensus reality wasn't a sponge bob show and earth hadn't the shape of a car. Just like we can't exactly prove this in real life, there is absolutely no evidence to back this up. The burden of proof belongs to whom claim those things.<br /> <br /> All you could show is that consensus is a fundamental part of reality, which i nwver disagreed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have to. It's not my claim. I don't care in the slightest what reality was like before people. My claim was that the consensus determines reality, which it does, and that means it can change reality, which it does. That's the foundations of Mage. It's spelled out in every core book and numerous supplements. The flat earth, the four humours, all of that was to illustrate just what consensual reality means, what kind of world Mage is. The consensus can change the world.<br /> <br /> You could have just said the flat earth was too much for you, made it a special case, and ignored it. It's not like the writers haven't done that before. You didn't have to claim that Mage physics is <i>and always was</i> physics as we know it. But you made the extreme claim and now you can't back it up, and that's too bad. But you do not get to push a burden of proof on others when you can't even meet it yourself. That is not an argument in good faith, and I'm going to stop taking you seriously if you keep making it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Technology doesn't work on those regions because consensus there makes it hard, just like the swiming against the river analogy. This has nothing to do with consensus actively changing reality itself, it's just making it harder for someone to make the change. There must be a &quot;mage&quot; trying to change the reality by using the technology. This example doesn't help your cause. </div> </div> </div>I didn't say technomagic or enlightened science,Mundane technology that any sleeper can use without the assistance of a mage often stops working in the remote areas of the world. Sleeper technology like cell phones require the consensus to work. Again, this is in the books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It does. When you consider that tje wod is similar to ours. Hell, even a D&amp;D universe follow the premises of our physics. If some claim must be made is that it is different, and Mage only claims this when dealing with magick and consensus. </div> </div> </div>Why would a different game by a different publisher entirely have any bearing on this situation?<br /> <br /> I honestly think we are done here. This is Mage, a game known far and wide for its strange setting and stranger metaphysics and you keep expecting it to behave normally. Your own assumptions are getting in your way at this point, and I don't see that changing any time soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 09-15-2016, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T18:56:41-07:00","id":970383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=970125#post970125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't have to. It's not my claim. I don't care in the slightest what reality was like before people.</div> </div> </div> </div>You claimed that earth was flat before people got to know it was round. But this is not the issue of our debate. The degree of interaction of consensus is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=970125#post970125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My claim was that the consensus determines reality, which it does, and that means it can change reality, which it does. That's the foundations of Mage. It's spelled out in every core book and numerous supplements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never said it wasn't. I agree with everything said here. Consensus can affect reality. Realisty isn't created by consensus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=970125#post970125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The flat earth, the four humours, all of that was to illustrate just what consensual reality means, what kind of world Mage is. The consensus can change the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can change the world by making changes in the world easier or harder. Not directly making the changes themselves. We already have been through this, we both can't efficiently prove our points since the books are too vague about how much power the consensus have indeed. It is purposely writen this way to give the ST freedom to make it the way he wants, like a lot of things in storyteller.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=970125#post970125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could have just said the flat earth was too much for you, made it a special case, and ignored it. It's not like the writers haven't done that before. You didn't have to claim that Mage physics is <i>and always was</i> physics as we know it. But you made the extreme claim and now you can't back it up, and that's too bad. But you do not get to push a burden of proof on others when you can't even meet it yourself. That is not an argument in good faith, and I'm going to stop taking you seriously if you keep making it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I already showed you my proof. The WoD universe is just like ours unless stated otherwise, you are the one trying to say that things are different, of course the burden of proof is yours. It's like saying that I have the burden of proving that unicorns doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=970125#post970125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say technomagic or enlightened science,Mundane technology that any sleeper can use without the assistance of a mage often stops working in the remote areas of the world. Sleeper technology like cell phones require the consensus to work. Again, this is in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that, that's why i used &quot;&quot; in &quot;mage&quot;. My argument stands. It is consensus of that area pushing the guy using the technology to the other side of the reality river. Technology was once magick, you know.. This is the kind of thing consensus can do, and it's supose to do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=970125#post970125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would a different game by a different publisher entirely have any bearing on this situation?</div> </div> </div> </div>All I was trying to do was that at default in any hystory, movie, etc. we take as default our own universe, unless stated otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=970125#post970125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly think we are done here. This is Mage, a game known far and wide for its strange setting and stranger metaphysics and you keep expecting it to behave normally. Your own assumptions are getting in your way at this point, and I don't see that changing any time soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. We just disagree on this aspect (consensus power) and have nothing but a couple of very generic quotes that isn't so much to back both our claims. Let's agree to disagree. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T00:10:21-07:00","id":970542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=969888#post969888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wtf? I was in the planwt last thursday and the planet too. By logic, this meams that the planet was created before. Please, start using logic.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your memory is false, then it could be that the planet in fact was not there. And you neither.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=969900#post969900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a common logical fallacy often associated with Creation myths. The idea being that an entity so powerful and detail oriented to be able to create your memories along with everything else. It is one of the reasons why Creation myths come with specific beginnings, to prevent people from descending into madness by questioning the validity of their own existence. <br /> <br /> It is also a common argument that people who believe in the intellectual infancy of solipsism retreat to (the 'you only exist because I believe that you exist' line of thinking). At best, it is used as the retreat of people who think they are philosophers but have not really bothered to spend time thinking about philosophy. At worst, it is the argument of sociopaths and psychopaths who lack the ability to come up with something creative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some people would read this as insulting...<br /> <br /> If I would believe in solipsism, then I would just ignore it because you know: I only have good reasons to believe that I am real (which is the better definition).<br /> <br /> I made this point because it highlights a critical point: How can you prove that the observer does not influence the observed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T04:51:02-07:00","id":970621,"title":"","content":"In science and philosophy, the burden of proof falls on the more extraordinary claim. Which is more extraordinary claim? That our memories were created by experience, our species by evolution, our world by geology? Or that some bearded fellow (or a sentient lasagna or whatever) created the world last Tuesday? <br /> <br /> The problem with any Creation myth, whether it has the trappings of religion or science, is that they all require extraordinary claims that are impossible to proven experimentally. The religious ones that depend on dieties can at least be justified as symbolic explanations of reality derived from the life experiences of ancient peoples and, if considered logically, are relatively harmless and may be beautifully poetic. The scientific ones that depend on exotic substances are just confusing and poorly justified, as we have not been able to find one microgram of dark matter or generate one erg of dark energy. <br /> <br /> Logic suggests that there was no Beginning, because there would have to be a Before, and that there will be no End, because there will have to be an After. Until we can generate experimental proof for the extraordinary claims of any Creation myth, they should all be treated with skepticism. The majority of the religious ones can be rejected out of hand though, as we have experimental evidence or experiential evidence that contradicts them. There are no oceans of milk or water beyond the clouds, the world is not composed of a handful of elements, and humans are genetically derived from more than two people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T09:19:39-07:00","id":970740,"title":"","content":"Seriously, Revan, there are so many things wrong with what you just posted that I'd have to chop it into little pieces to deal with it all and I'm done with that. You somehow conflate 'the earth when people believed it was flat' with 'the earth before people,' you somehow conflate 'the consensus determines reality' with 'the consensus affects reality, and possibly not all that much.' You completely ignore any explanation of how you are reading lines wrong or reading in interpretations that just weren't there. Oh right, and you just tried to inflict a burden of proof you weren't willing to live by. Your claim deviates much further from &quot;Material reality is a consensual hallucination that the vast majority of humanity agrees on&quot; than mine deviates from &quot;the world of mages seems like our own.&quot;<br /> <br /> So yeah, we're probably going to have to agree to disagree. It's only mildly different from disagreeing to disagree anyways.<br /> <br /> But before we drop this for good, I do want to follow up on one thing I'm curious about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=970383#post970383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that, that's why i used &quot;&quot; in &quot;mage&quot;. My argument stands. It is consensus of that area pushing the guy using the technology to the other side of the reality river. Technology was once magick, you know.. This is the kind of thing consensus can do, and it's supose to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>You just admitted that magic can become mundane technology (which already contradicts what you said earlier, but whatever). So when a laptop fails because it gets outside the consensus, some part of the way it works stops behaving the way it should. What do you think changes? Do electrons change their behavior? Do the materials that control their flow and timing stop directing them? Do the electrons cease to exist entirely? I'm curious what you think happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T05:27:00-07:00","id":971263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=970621#post970621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In science and philosophy, the burden of proof falls on the more extraordinary claim.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a mage context I am tempted to say that the \u201cphysics is fundamental reality\u201c is the more extraordinary claim.<br /> <br /> It takes more assumptions than the \u201creality is shaped by belief alone\u201c","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12022,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","user":"Nonsense","date":". 09-17-2016, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T06:18:33-07:00","id":971286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=968356#post968356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with that position, and many of the other subjective positions offered by a lot of Mage players, is that they are implicitly bigoted positions that justify oppression and genocide. I will explain.</div> </div> </div> </div> I contend that it is ultimately a far more bigoted position to suggest that the opinions of non-whites, women and the Native Americans matter less than those of &quot;straight white men&quot;, which is what you are implying when you suggest that consensus would be defined by the views of the latter and not by <i>everyone, </i>which is the point of Mage to a degree. Everybody believes in something, and everybody's beliefs matter.<br /> <br /> I would be inclined to suspect that the Natives didn't think of themselves as inferior, to say nothing of... well, <i>everybody else</i>. Do their opinions not matter?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=968356#post968356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Consensus of the Old World before the 1400s said that there were no unknown continents, so the Americas were not thought to exist. If the Consensus shapes reality, then the Americas did not exist before the 1400s and the Americas were created to be conquered by European men and, by extension, the Native Americans were created to be the victims of European men. If the Consensus iust shapes magic, then the Americas existed before the 1400s and European men were just genocidal maniacs.</div> </div> </div> </div> When you say things like this, you're indulging in some subtle bigotry yourself; in doing so, are you not divesting non-Europeans of agency and, indeed, casting them solely in the role of victims to be exploited by expeditious imperialists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11105,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11105-seviphas","user":"Seviphas","date":". 09-17-2016, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11105-seviphas","name":"Seviphas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T06:52:12-07:00","id":971305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=971263#post971263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In a mage context I am tempted to say that the \u201cphysics is fundamental reality\u201c is the more extraordinary claim.<br /> <br /> It takes more assumptions than the \u201creality is shaped by belief alone\u201c</div> </div> </div> </div>Hardly. Experimental evidence, verified by thousands of experiments that were desperately trying to find an error in the foundational theories, supports the majority of the positions. What evidence do you have that the belief of human beings have changed the physics of the world or really anything? The majority of humans believe that in a benevolent diety, but there is precious little evidence of that belief being worth anything throughout history.<br /> <br /> As for the Native American issue, it is the weight of numbers. The best estimates have the population of the New World in the 1400s being 25% of that of the population of the Old World. Unless the paradoxical position is taken that the number of people who believe in something has no impact on how the Consensus shapes reality, the fact that 80% of the people believed that there was open water between England and Japan meant that the Consensus (if it shapes reality) should have long ago destroyed the Americas. It logically follows then that either a) the Concensus shapes reality and America was created by the European Consensus to serve European needs or b) the Consensus does not shape reality and the Americas have always been there. Since there has never been experimental evidence of belief shaping reality, b) is presumed to be correct.<br /> <br /> On another note, while it is a common fallacy that European people thought that the Earth was flat until Columbus, that is not true. It was well known fact that Europeans had known that the Earth was a sphere since the time of Pythagoros, 6th century BC, and that only lunatics believed in a Flat Earth by the 8th century AD. While the idea had spread throught the Old World through the trade networks that connected to Europe by the 2nd century AD, there were some minor religious communities that believed in a Flat Earth took a while to be convinced. In fact, the support for the hypothesis of a spherical Earth was one of the first recorded scientific experiments in human history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T08:28:24-07:00","id":971331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=971305#post971305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hardly. Experimental evidence, verified by thousands of experiments that were desperately trying to find an error in the foundational theories, supports the majority of the positions. What evidence do you have that the belief of human beings have changed the physics of the world or really anything? The majority of humans believe that in a benevolent diety, but there is precious little evidence of that belief being worth anything throughout history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is a potentially reasonable argument for our world, but isn't relevant here because Nonsense specifically said 'in Mage.' When core books say that anything believed hard enough becomes static reality, it really shifts the balance of what is an extraordinary claim*.<br /> <br /> *In fact the existence of the books is the only reason I would even invoke the term 'extraordinary claim.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the Native American issue, it is the weight of numbers. The best estimates have the population of the New World in the 1400s being 25% of that of the population of the Old World. Unless the paradoxical position is taken that the number of people who believe in something has no impact on how the Consensus shapes reality, the fact that 80% of the people believed that there was open water between England and Japan meant that the Consensus (if it shapes reality) should have long ago destroyed the Americas. It logically follows then that either a) the Concensus shapes reality and America was created by the European Consensus to serve European needs or b) the Consensus does not shape reality and the Americas have always been there. Since there has never been experimental evidence of belief shaping reality, b) is presumed to be correct. </div> </div> </div>Or c) they weren't close enough to the Americas to affect them in any significant way. Or d) there was still so much unexplored territory in the world that no one believed they had found everything. Or most importantly e) the Consensus can't imagine away its constituent parts.<br /> <br /> You can't just say a Consensus with these X qualities doesn't exist, therefore a Consensus doesn't exist, especially when we already have reason to suspect it doesn't have X qualities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On another note, while it is a common fallacy that European people thought that the Earth was flat until Columbus, that is not true. It was well known fact that Europeans had known that the Earth was a sphere since the time of Pythagoros, 6th century BC, and that only lunatics believed in a Flat Earth by the 8th century AD. While the idea had spread throught the Old World through the trade networks that connected to Europe by the 2nd century AD, there were some minor religious communities that believed in a Flat Earth took a while to be convinced. In fact, the support for the hypothesis of a spherical Earth was one of the first recorded scientific experiments in human history. </div> </div> </div>Thank you for that. That fallacy always bugs me and I specifically called out Ancient Greece in the flat earth example for that reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 09-17-2016, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T11:10:23-07:00","id":971414,"title":"","content":"It is of course noted in Sorcerer's Crusade that some people do in fact circumnavigate the globe without hitting the Americas, simply passing through a large stretch of open sea before arriving at China. The mapmakers had not yet established its position, so reality remained mutable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T13:07:09-07:00","id":971485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=971414#post971414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is of course noted in Sorcerer's Crusade that some people do in fact circumnavigate the globe without hitting the Americas, simply passing through a large stretch of open sea before arriving at China. The mapmakers had not yet established its position, so reality remained mutable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! That's what I was looking for. I was pretty sure distance and direction between civilizations used to be fluid until the Void Seekers locked it in place. I just don't have sorcerer's crusade so I couldn't check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T19:42:10-07:00","id":971682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=970740#post970740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, Revan, there are so many things wrong with what you just posted that I'd have to chop it into little pieces to deal with it all and I'm done with that. You somehow conflate 'the earth when people believed it was flat' with 'the earth before people,' you somehow conflate 'the consensus determines reality' with 'the consensus affects reality, and possibly not all that much.' You completely ignore any explanation of how you are reading lines wrong or reading in interpretations that just weren't there. Oh right, and you just tried to inflict a burden of proof you weren't willing to live by. Your claim deviates much further from &quot;Material reality is a consensual hallucination that the vast majority of humanity agrees on&quot; than mine deviates from &quot;the world of mages seems like our own.&quot;<br /> <br /> So yeah, we're probably going to have to agree to disagree. It's only mildly different from disagreeing to disagree anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Aya Tari said, the burden of proof lies in the most extraordinary claim. Not in-game, as to Mage anything is extraordinary (or nothing?). I have shown you proof that WoD is similar to our universe, and even without that quote, the default is to make it similar to our own. If this wasn`t the default, and the authors haven`t cited that similarity, then each and every game universe would be <b>completely</b> different and imossible to even discuss about, since every player would be following different rules of physics. You`d come up in this forum asking how to make an effect and someone would say that you need X sphere because, in his game, the universe works Y way.<br /> <br /> Accept it, our universe is the default, feel free to change it though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=970740#post970740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But before we drop this for good, I do want to follow up on one thing I'm curious about.<br /> <br /> You just admitted that magic can become mundane technology (which already contradicts what you said earlier, but whatever). So when a laptop fails because it gets outside the consensus, some part of the way it works stops behaving the way it should. What do you think changes? Do electrons change their behavior? Do the materials that control their flow and timing stop directing them? Do the electrons cease to exist entirely? I'm curious what you think happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course I admited. Sigh, you seem to not yet understand how I think about Mage's reality at all. It doesn`t contradict anything. Come on, it's not that hard to understand: Consensus can alter how changes are made, how easy it is to make. Magick becaming mundane technology just means that Consensus now understands that that focus and effect is acceptable, so it is so easy to do it that no longer needs an Enlightned Will nor magick to happen. Got it?<br /> <br /> Well, M20 got pretty clear that Reality Zones is optional and will work according to ST decision. Myself, if I were to implement this idea, physics wouldn`t stop working, electrons still exists and works the way they should. Same for the device components. What makes it fail is simply the Consensus itself making it harder for the device to work (remember when I said that Consensus can dictate if some action is possible or not, thus making it easier or harder to do?). That`s it. Consensus would act as a force of the universe preventing the technology to work without some Enlightened Will to force it upon reality.<br /> <br /> It seems that you that haven't understood what I think about Consensus...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the Native American issue, it is the weight of numbers. The best estimates have the population of the New World in the 1400s being 25% of that of the population of the Old World. Unless the paradoxical position is taken that the number of people who believe in something has no impact on how the Consensus shapes reality, the fact that 80% of the people believed that there was open water between England and Japan meant that the Consensus (if it shapes reality) should have long ago destroyed the Americas. It logically follows then that either a) the Concensus shapes reality and America was created by the European Consensus to serve European needs or b) the Consensus does not shape reality and the Americas have always been there. Since there has never been experimental evidence of belief shaping reality, b) is presumed to be correct. </div> </div> </div>THIS!! Just this!! This is the kind of power that Consensus <b>does not have </b>that people are giving it. Perfect example Aya, thanks!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or c) they weren't close enough to the Americas to affect them in any significant way.. </div> </div> </div>So, now people have to be close to the subject of belief? How close are people from breast cancer? And from massive black holes in the center of the galaxy? According to this logic Consensus couldn't affect anything outside the planet. I thought you said it determines entire reality...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or d) there was still so much unexplored territory in the world that no one believed they had found everything </div> </div> </div>Doesn`t make a difference. They didn`t know about americas existence, therefore Americas shouldn't exist, just like atoms and breast cancer, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or most importantly e) the Consensus can't imagine away its constituent parts.<br /> <br /> You can't just say a Consensus with these X qualities doesn't exist, therefore a Consensus doesn't exist, especially when we already have reason to suspect it doesn't have X qualities </div> </div> </div>Dindn`t followed that... He didn`t said Consensus doesn`t exists...<br /> <br /> Ramnesis, I think the main issue you're having interpreting those quotes is that &quot;determine&quot; means to decide. Consensus is the ultimate judge to decide if something is vulgar or coincident, if something is mundane or magickal. It doesn't generates reality itself. Reality is older than Consensus, afterall.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T23:25:32-07:00","id":971789,"title":"","content":"Discussing this is really fun, thank you!<br /> <br /> I do not think that it is as simple as a poll.<br /> 80 percent think X and 20 percent think Y. How should it not be possible for Reality to express both?<br /> <br /> It is the humans who get problems understanding that something is a particle and a wave at the same time...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T00:14:52-07:00","id":971802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=971682#post971682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As Aya Tari said, the burden of proof lies in the most extraordinary claim. Not in-game, as to Mage anything is extraordinary (or nothing?). I have shown you proof that WoD is similar to our universe, and even without that quote, the default is to make it similar to our own. If this wasn`t the default, and the authors haven`t cited that similarity, then each and every game universe would be <b>completely</b> different and imossible to even discuss about, since every player would be following different rules of physics. You`d come up in this forum asking how to make an effect and someone would say that you need X sphere because, in his game, the universe works Y way.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is nothing like watching someone offer up an argument that actually contradicts itself. In our world, so far as we know, throwing fireballs by chanting in Enochian is impossible. Saying it could happen would be the extraordinary claim. Yet you have no problem with the idea that it can happen in Mage because, of course, the book says that it can. So even you accept that it's the game line and not our reality that determines what can happen and what is an extraordinary claim.<br /> <br /> When it suits you, anyways...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course I admited. Sigh, you seem to not yet understand how I think about Mage's reality at all. It doesn`t contradict anything. Come on, it's not that hard to understand: Consensus can alter how changes are made, how easy it is to make. Magick becaming mundane technology just means that Consensus now understands that that focus and effect is acceptable, so it is so easy to do it that no longer needs an Enlightned Will nor magick to happen. Got it? </div> </div> </div>So electrons always existed but until the Consensus realized it, but they didn't, what... flow? Or is the idea that laptops are just an effect and there's nothing special about what is happening inside? Break this down for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Myself, if I were to implement this idea, physics wouldn`t stop working, electrons still exists and works the way they should. </div> </div> </div>I'd give you credit for at least admitting that it's something other than modern physics that are the baseline reality for Mage, but I have no doubt you will walk this back once you realize you said it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> THIS!! Just this!! This is the kind of power that Consensus <b>does not have </b>that people are giving it. Perfect example Aya, thanks! </div> </div> </div>Who, other than you and Aya, are giving this power to the Consensus?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, now people have to be close to the subject of belief? How close are people from breast cancer? And from massive black holes in the center of the galaxy? According to this logic Consensus couldn't affect anything outside the planet. I thought you said it determines entire reality... </div> </div> </div>You just finished talking about Reality Zones, Revan. You literally cannot be ignorant enough to make this argument.<br /> <br /> At this point you are willing to contradict yourself to try to win.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 09-18-2016, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T07:49:09-07:00","id":971926,"title":"","content":"I think it should be important to note that the various mage books were written by different authors and many books within the same edition contradict each other. If one were to read all of them and try to make all of them equally cannon, you'd get nothing but conflicting evidence and a migraine. I'm sure some authors also believed in a static mage reality while others believed in fully consensual reality. All evidence to support either can be brushed aside as a mage unconsciously using true magick to get reality to fit their paradigm or work of a multi layer reality governed by belief. In the end its like being a mage, fiercely believing a concept without any evidence to prove it exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T09:56:59-07:00","id":971979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=971926#post971926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it should be important to note that the various mage books were written by different authors and many books within the same edition contradict each other. If one were to read all of them and try to make all of them equally cannon, you'd get nothing but conflicting evidence and a migraine. I'm sure some authors also believed in a static mage reality while others believed in fully consensual reality. All evidence to support either can be brushed aside as a mage unconsciously using true magick to get reality to fit their paradigm or work of a multi layer reality governed by belief. In the end its like being a mage, fiercely believing a concept without any evidence to prove it exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something you always have to deal with in Mage However, if you ignore something you have to say what and why, otherwise you are just needlessly confusing things. Also, depending on how much you are setting aside, you may be going far beyond interpretation and into house rule territory.<br /> <br /> I often call out the Time Travel Paradox rules as nonsensical and refuse to use them, because I see them as an unnecessary kludge based on false equivalence. It's undeniably a house rule, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T10:06:57-07:00","id":971983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=971802#post971802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is nothing like watching someone offer up an argument that actually contradicts itself. In our world, so far as we know, throwing fireballs by chanting in Enochian is impossible. Saying it could happen would be the extraordinary claim. Yet you have no problem with the idea that it can happen in Mage because, of course, the book says that it can. So even you accept that it's the game line and not our reality that determines what can happen and what is an extraordinary claim.<br /> <br /> When it suits you, anyways...</div> </div> </div> </div>No contradiction at all. Again, you failed to understand my point. I wonder if it is I that am not so well versed in english, or you who just doesn`t want to understand.<br /> I am pretty sure that I said that the default is that WoD is like our universe, <b>unless stated otherwise</b>. They say that mages can cast fireballs. This makes WoD just like our world, but with people casting fireballs. But they also say mages can fly, become invisible and do virtually anything! So, WoD is just like our universe, but with mages making any kind of effect. And then they talk about paradox, Avatars, etc. So, all those kind of things exist in WoD. What they don`t say is that reality is a creation of Consensus. Nor that Consensus can make such big effect on reality, all they say is that Consesnsus shape reality, and determines when something is considererd vulgar or not. It`s the nth time I say this and yet you still think I`m contradicting myself...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=971802#post971802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So electrons always existed but until the Consensus realized it, but they didn't, what... flow? Or is the idea that laptops are just an effect and there's nothing special about what is happening inside? Break this down for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before Consensus knew about electrons, they existed and flow just like they should.The laptop simply didn`t worked because Consensus didn`t let it work, unless a Enlightened Will forced it to. Again, this is my take on this matter, and isn't the right answer. There is no right answer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=971802#post971802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd give you credit for at least admitting that it's something other than modern physics that are the baseline reality for Mage, but I have no doubt you will walk this back once you realize you said it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wtf?! Is like talking to a door. I repeatedly said that there is a Consensus that influence in reality. Again, our world physics is the default laws of WoD. Add on top of this all the supernatural things they say in the books. Again, we don't disagree of the baselines of Mage, but what is the Consensus capable of doing...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=971802#post971802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who, other than you and Aya, are giving this power to the Consensus?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are in the moment you say that Consensus is able to change the shape of the planet, or change how the very building blocks of reality are made, like the existence of atoms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=971802#post971802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You just finished talking about Reality Zones, Revan. You literally cannot be ignorant enough to make this argument.<br /> <br /> At this point you are willing to contradict yourself to try to win.</div> </div> </div> </div>My argument is that Consensus can't make effects. REality zones are just areas where some effects are considered vulgar. That's the power Consensus have. When you start giving Consensus the pwer to make effects, you have problems like the ones Aya posted.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T11:14:41-07:00","id":972024,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I have to agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3153_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3153\" data-vbnamecard=\"3153\">Lord Revan</a> about the Consensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T11:59:57-07:00","id":972053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=971983#post971983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No contradiction at all. Again, you failed to understand my point. I wonder if it is I that am not so well versed in english, or you who just doesn`t want to understand.<br /> I am pretty sure that I said that the default is that WoD is like our universe, <b>unless stated otherwise</b>. They say that mages can cast fireballs. This makes WoD just like our world, but with people casting fireballs. But they also say mages can fly, become invisible and do virtually anything!</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't actually know you weren't well versed in English, but it does explain some this communication problem we've been having. I don't think that's the only problem here, though. The bigger issue is you are also unwilling to even consider points of view you don't like.<br /> <br /> So you say that Mage is like our world unless stated otherwise, and that is true. But then you ignore parts of the book that state otherwise, like &quot;the mass of our Earth's reality comes from the belief of the sleepers or &quot;beliefs structure material reality,&quot; or the Sorcerers Crusade line about people sometimes being able to sail from Europe to Asia without hitting the Americas. Those lines mean something too. You are free to ignore them, but you cannot then say you are using the default play style.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, this is my take on this matter, and isn't the right answer. There is no right answer. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, our world physics is the default laws of WoD. </div> </div> </div>Are you even aware that these two things are completely different claims? Electrons and their behavior are part of real world physics. If there is no real answer to why they stop working there is no real answer to if they work in the first place.<br /> <br /> This is why it is impossible to discuss anything with you. You admit there's no right answer one moment, then insist you are using the one true way the next. When you figure out which one it is, maybe there will be something to discuss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T13:48:07-07:00","id":972104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=972053#post972053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't actually know you weren't well versed in English, but it does explain some this communication problem we've been having. I don't think that's the only problem here, though. The bigger issue is you are also unwilling to even consider points of view you don't like.<br /> <br /> So you say that Mage is like our world unless stated otherwise, and that is true. But then you ignore parts of the book that state otherwise, like &quot;the mass of our Earth's reality comes from the belief of the sleepers or &quot;beliefs structure material reality,&quot; or the Sorcerers Crusade line about people sometimes being able to sail from Europe to Asia without hitting the Americas. Those lines mean something too. You are free to ignore them, but you cannot then say you are using the default play style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beliefs structure material reality by making actions vulgar or coincident. Making things possible or impossible. Not by making things. I`m not familiar with Sorcerers Crusade.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=972053#post972053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you even aware that these two things are completely different claims? Electrons and their behavior are part of real world physics. If there is no real answer to why they stop working there is no real answer to if they work in the first place.<br /> <br /> This is why it is impossible to discuss anything with you. You admit there's no right answer one moment, then insist you are using the one true way the next. When you figure out which one it is, maybe there will be something to discuss.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they are not, because you took them from different discussions. The first one is my take on the optional rule of reality zones, which indeed is up to ST. the second one is my opinion abut Mage reality, which I take as default because it is the same we have in real life, plus the things they added in the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:13:23-07:00","id":972150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=972104#post972104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beliefs structure material reality by making actions vulgar or coincident. Making things possible or impossible. Not by making things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Say it enough times it might even become true. This is Mage after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The second one is my opinion abut Mage reality, which I take as default because it is the same we have in real life, plus the things they added in the system. </div> </div> </div>Minus the things which are in the system that Revan doesn't like.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T23:31:35-07:00","id":972367,"title":"","content":"A close reading of the reality zones rules reveals that they technically only apply to Awakened Magick: they determine where the line between Coincidental and Vulgar lies, and they possibly give an additional \u00b11 difficulty modifier if the Magick resonates with or against the zone. Note that physics and biology arguably aren't Vulgar <i>or</i> Coincidental. A case can be made that reality zones are entirely about what people believe, and have nothing to do with how reality actually works. The section on Technocratic reality even goes so far as to say that the Union has an advantage in part because what they believe aligns with actual physics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T00:21:45-07:00","id":972379,"title":"","content":"Consensus cannot be wrong. Consensus is global belief, sometimes separated into different reality zones.<br /> <br /> If certain reality zone has people that believe people can fly, then Mages can fly there and do so coincidentally, despite the fact that gravity dictates you cannot.<br /> <br /> Mage is a game of belief, keep that in mind. Consensus simply cannot be wrong, because it is not as closely tied to actual laws of Earth as you might think. It's all about belief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T05:51:03-07:00","id":972464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=972367#post972367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A close reading of the reality zones rules reveals that they technically only apply to Awakened Magick: they determine where the line between Coincidental and Vulgar lies, and they possibly give an additional \u00b11 difficulty modifier if the Magick resonates with or against the zone. Note that physics and biology arguably aren't Vulgar <i>or</i> Coincidental. A case can be made that reality zones are entirely about what people believe, and have nothing to do with how reality actually works. The section on Technocratic reality even goes so far as to say that the Union has an advantage in part because what they believe aligns with actual physics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's the hallmark of the Technocracy's isn't it. Many of the Traditions paradigms don't need reality to be a certain way (e.g. God can heal someone regardless of if medicine is based on cellular biology or the four humours). The party line of the Technocracy, though, is that they are using the laws of the world, so they will change them in their favor if they can. <br /> <br /> Note that Primal Reality Zones are also stated as possible default states for the Reality of the World.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 09-19-2016, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T07:13:20-07:00","id":972498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=972150#post972150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Say it enough times it might even become true. This is Mage after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Show me one example of Consensus actively making changes in rea\u00e7ity other than making it harder or easier to cast effects and unbelief making effects disappear in Mage the Ascension, please.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=972150#post972150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minus the things which are in the system that Revan doesn't like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like what? What is explicitly stated in the books that I'm failing to acknowledge? Please just don't bring back those quotes that we know that don't confirm anything.<br /> <br /> Dataweaver, you are completely right. That information on technocratic reality confirm even more my view of defult reality adopted in Mage. Also, you're right again about reality zone just making things vulgar or coincident. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T07:28:49-07:00","id":972512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=972498#post972498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Show me one example of Consensus actively making changes in rea\u00e7ity other than making it harder or easier to cast effects and unbelief making effects disappear in Mage the Ascension, please.<br /> <br /> <br /> Like what? What is explicitly stated in the books that I'm failing to acknowledge? Please just don't bring back those quotes that we know that don't confirm anything.<br /> <br /> Dataweaver, you are completely right. That information on technocratic reality confirm even more my view of defult reality adopted in Mage. Also, you're right again about reality zone just making things vulgar or coincident. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Geography. Geography wasn't set until the Void Seekers made it set.<br /> <br /> Space. 'Outer Space' didn't exist before the Void Engineers made it so.<br /> <br /> And while they do have format space, and make use of it, their preferred method of doing these things? Bringing along sleepers and letting the slow battering ram of their beliefs trample the universe into place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T12:22:04-07:00","id":972637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=972498#post972498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Show me one example of Consensus actively making changes in rea\u00e7ity other than making it harder or easier to cast effects and unbelief making effects disappear in Mage the Ascension, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>The laptop mentioned earlier...<br /> <br /> Either way it is an effect of the consensus, wether it makes it work or it prevents it from working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T19:33:27-07:00","id":972885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=972512#post972512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Geography. Geography wasn't set until the Void Seekers made it set.<br /> <br /> Space. 'Outer Space' didn't exist before the Void Engineers made it so.<br /> <br /> And while they do have format space, and make use of it, their preferred method of doing these things? Bringing along sleepers and letting the slow battering ram of their beliefs trample the universe into place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that objective canon or subjective fluff? Is it a Void Engineer or Technocrats claiming that? If so, that is Technocracy subjectivity. Is it verified in other gamelines? If not, it is Mage subjectivity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T05:05:56-07:00","id":973044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=972512#post972512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Geography. Geography wasn't set until the Void Seekers made it set.<br /> <br /> Space. 'Outer Space' didn't exist before the Void Engineers made it so.<br /> <br /> And while they do have format space, and make use of it, their preferred method of doing these things? Bringing along sleepers and letting the slow battering ram of their beliefs trample the universe into place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think space always existed, but was considered another dimension, like Umbra. What Consensus changed, was making it coincident place. Also, Umbra and other dimensions follow theirbown rules. I am discussing earth laws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T05:06:46-07:00","id":973045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=972637#post972637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The laptop mentioned earlier...<br /> <br /> Either way it is an effect of the consensus, wether it makes it work or it prevents it from working.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you serious? This is the only kind of change the consensus make that I'm defending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T07:11:24-07:00","id":973113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=972498#post972498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like what? What is explicitly stated in the books that I'm failing to acknowledge? Please just don't bring back those quotes that we know that don't confirm anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>You just asked what is in the books that you are failing to acknowledge, other than the stuff you are failing to acknowledge. Deal with the stuff on your plate before asking for desert.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I was actually holding off responding to you to see if you were going to ignore this one:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=972512#post972512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geography. Geography wasn't set until the Void Seekers made it set.</div> </div> </div> </div>True to form, you did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=972637#post972637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The laptop mentioned earlier...<br /> <br /> Either way it is an effect of the consensus, wether it makes it work or it prevents it from working.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=973045#post973045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you serious? This is the only kind of change the consensus make that I'm defending.</div> </div> </div> </div>But here's the big thing I missed before. Look at where Laptops stop working. It's not in population centers, it's in the distant places of the world with low or no population. Laptops stop working where the Consensus is weak. That means it is the Consensus that makes them work, not the Consensus that stops them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T07:25:09-07:00","id":973125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=973045#post973045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you serious? This is the only kind of change the consensus make that I'm defending.</div> </div> </div> </div>How are other effects different (other than in magnitude/scope)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T12:03:53-07:00","id":973277,"title":"","content":"With all due respect, I've seen several claims here about technology falling in different regions of the world; but in my reading of M20 the only thing remotely like that that I've found is mention that techno<i>magick</i> tends to fail in primal zones. Not \u201ctechnology\u201d; \u201ctechnomagick\u201d. The assertion that a laptop would fail deep in the Amazon Jungle appears to be based on the assumption that these two things are in fact one and the same; and while that <i>is</i> a valid assumption to make, it's not an established fact. Note that every example given in the Reality Zones section speaks of the effect of the zone on <i>magick</i>, techno or otherwise. There are no examples that I'm aware of that describe, say, the laws of physics changing in a Reality Zone. If you find one, please post a page reference and quote the part in question.<br /> <br /> As for Format Space: that doesn't create conventional space, per se; it erects a Gauntlet between conventional space and the Umbra where no such barrier previously existed, isolating the Umbra and its laws from conventional space. I'll grant that that's a bit more than just changing the Vulgarity or difficulty of magick; but it's not exactly altering the laws of physics either. And it's also from a Revised sourcebook (albeit a late one), not M20; so its validity isn't a foregone conclusion. It's <i>probably</i> valid; but I can't guarantee it. <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> All that said: I'm partial the idea that the Consensus <i>does</i> potentially alter the laws of reality \u2014 in small ways, and only when a significant portion of the population's beliefs are aligned. This is most commonly known as <i>mythic threads</i>; and other than being another thing that alters the difficulty of magick, its only known effect is as a possible enabler of hedge magic. Remember, the Consensus is the cumulative effect of Sleeping Avatars; I don't see it being able to achieve anything an Arete \u00b7\u00b7 mage can't do with sufficient successes, if that; and even there, I wouldn't expect much in the way of successes. These are <i>Sleeping</i> Avatars, after all; any <i>actual</i> changes would have to be based on something to the effect of Wild Magick. It can mess with Awakened Magick, but not much beyond that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T12:32:04-07:00","id":973296,"title":"","content":"What enables technology (example: guns) to work in the present? Because in the past they did not work for sleepers. In my understanding it is first possible for mages to do strange things before it is safe for sleepers. If it is not the consensus something else must be it.<br /> <br /> I like Sorcerers Crusade, and there you have a variety of tech and it is a paradox magnet.<br /> Mystics and Faithful Ones have it easy and Technomancers get doxed for using things that get usable for sleepers some time later.<br /> <br /> I am sorry for not being able to deliver quotes at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T12:46:56-07:00","id":973307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=973277#post973277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all due respect, I've seen several claims here about technology falling in different regions of the world; but in my reading of M20 the only thing remotely like that that I've found is mention that techno<i>magick</i> tends to fail in primal zones. Not \u201ctechnology\u201d; \u201ctechnomagick\u201d. The assertion that a laptop would fail deep in the Amazon Jungle appears to be based on the assumption that these two things are in fact one and the same; and while that <i>is</i> a valid assumption to make, it's not an established fact. Note that every example given in the Reality Zones section speaks of the effect of the zone on <i>magick</i>, techno or otherwise. There are no examples that I'm aware of that describe, say, the laws of physics changing in a Reality Zone. If you find one, please post a page reference and quote the part in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>The section I was calling out was actually from M2nd. M20 does say, though, that &quot;Advanced technology tends to fail in deep-wilderness areas, but the oldest forms of magick thrive.&quot; (M20, pg 615).<br /> <br /> Again, my issue is not with some kind of unchangeable reality underlying the consensus. That's left as an open possibility in every edition I've read. It's not even with that underlying reality being modern physics. That's an awkward interpretation of the setting that takes a lot of shoehorning to make work, but if people want to play that way who am I to stop them. No, what I am contesting is that it is the default idea for Mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All that said: I'm partial the idea that the Consensus <i>does</i> potentially alter the laws of reality \u2014 in small ways, and only when a significant portion of the population's beliefs are aligned. This is most commonly known as <i>mythic threads</i>; and other than being another thing that alters the difficulty of magick, its only known effect is as a possible enabler of hedge magic. Remember, the Consensus is the cumulative effect of Sleeping Avatars; I don't see it being able to achieve anything an Arete \u00b7\u00b7 mage can't do with sufficient successes, if that; and even there, I wouldn't expect much in the way of successes. These are <i>Sleeping</i> Avatars, after all; any <i>actual</i> changes would have to be based on something to the effect of Wild Magick. It can mess with Awakened Magick, but not much beyond that. </div> </div> </div>Change small to unnoticeable and you aren't too far from my view of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T12:54:51-07:00","id":973314,"title":"","content":"The matter is complicated by the fact that a lot of modern consumer and super-high-end technology is heavily reliant on infrastructure to do much of anything - and anyplace that has a lot of technological infrastructure set up is by nature friendly to technomagick. The Sleepers' efforts there make it so. Cellphones don't work without cell towards. Electronics don't work without power sources. Most of the stuff designed to go into unfriendly environments is hardened or made more resilient in some fashion, and I imagine that in the WoD a lot of it essentially requires what amounts to an Extraordinary Citizen or an 'incursion' of a tiny bit of Consensus.<br /> <br /> So it's actually somewhat hard to distinguish between the &quot;Consensus can actually make things work or not work&quot; model - &quot;the Consensus is weak here, so technomagic like electrons and things that Technocrats assume like electrons don't work right&quot; like electrons that are how Technocrats work magick don't properly exist&quot; - from the technological paradigm - &quot;the tech isn't hardened against unfavorable environments and relies on infrastructure that's absent, what do you expect from consumer-grade crap/big hefty installations?&quot;<br /> <br /> The big factor in my mind is that in the Earth's Umbra, technology in general isn't reliable. It's basically a 'pristine' place where external laws aren't exposed except by the observer... which means that when you remove Consensus directly, you <i>don't</i> get nice objective stable modern physics etc., or even a refinement thereof. You get... weird subjective whatsis with only a few established commonalities.<br /> <br /> (And of course, the Consensus can't accomplish things outside the realm of a sufficient-Arete mage with a bunch of assistance couldn't... but then, considering what someone with Mastery of Life, Matter, Forces, Prime, Spirit, Mind, Entropy, Correspondence, and Time can pull off, let alone Archmasters? ...that is <i>not</i> very much of a constraint at all.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-20-2016, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:20:27-07:00","id":973345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=973307#post973307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The section I was calling out was actually from M2nd. M20 does say, though, that &quot;Advanced technology tends to fail in deep-wilderness areas, but the oldest forms of magick thrive.&quot; (M20, pg 615).<br /> <br /> Again, my issue is not with some kind of unchangeable reality underlying the consensus. That's left as an open possibility in every edition I've read. It's not even with that underlying reality being modern physics. That's an awkward interpretation of the setting that takes a lot of shoehorning to make work, but if people want to play that way who am I to stop them. No, what I am contesting is that it is the default idea for Mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Change small to unnoticeable and you aren't too far from my view of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. It makes sense that the Consensus would be restricted to imposing changes that would be Coincidental if a mage attempted them. That, and Consensus-imposed changes are always passive, ongoing effects that alter the ground rules more than actually doing anything. <br /> <br /> As for what the default is: I think it's best left in the Storyteller's hands. That said, if your chronicle is set in a shared world of darkness, then the Consensus is <i>not</i> always right. Vampires aren't subject to the Consensus. And even without that, there <i>are</i> the aforementioned Earthly Foundations. One way or the other, there are aspects of reality that do not conform to the Consensus, of anyone else. And this is a good thing; because otherwise, the Consensus would be to blame for such things as Climate Change, and I'd be looking askance at the VEs for choosing to make Conventional Space an inhospitable freezing, weightless vacuum. Some things are what they are just because, and not because anyone chose them to be that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:34:25-07:00","id":973354,"title":"","content":"@Quantumboost: my contention is that the Consensus can't do what a Master of even an Adept could do \u2014 or if it can, it requires a high-density population with a remarkably high consistency of beliefs. Certainly, a lot of Sleepers with shared beliefs can enact changes that a few Sleepers (or a lot of Sleepers with conflicting views) can't; and I'd be willing to hypothesize that this takes the form of a higher effective Arete in terms of what sorts of changes can be imposed. But even with that, I wouldn't take it as a given that the population densities needed for, say, Disciple-level changes (let alone Adept, Master, or Archmaster) can physically be achieved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T15:14:38-07:00","id":973424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=973345#post973345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. It makes sense that the Consensus would be restricted to imposing changes that would be Coincidental if a mage attempted them. That, and Consensus-imposed changes are always passive, ongoing effects that alter the ground rules more than actually doing anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly, yes. I prefer to think that all of reality is determined by the consensus, but that much of it is so deeply entrenched that it would be nigh impossible to change people's minds about it. I do think that significant, possibly fundamental changes are possible, but they have to be in realms people don't interact with or think about on a regular basis. This has gotten progressively harder as the realms that people can witness has grown. Changing the basic structure of life before the widespread use of microscopes may have been feasible. Changing it now is probably not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T15:44:49-07:00","id":973449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=973354#post973354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Quantumboost: my contention is that the Consensus can't do what a Master of even an Adept could do \u2014 or if it can, it requires a high-density population with a remarkably high consistency of beliefs. Certainly, a lot of Sleepers with shared beliefs can enact changes that a few Sleepers (or a lot of Sleepers with conflicting views) can't; and I'd be willing to hypothesize that this takes the form of a higher effective Arete in terms of what sorts of changes can be imposed. But even with that, I wouldn't take it as a given that the population densities needed for, say, Disciple-level changes (let alone Adept, Master, or Archmaster) can physically be achieved.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really think that's consistent with what the Consensus is supposed to be capable of.<br /> <br /> Consider just how many determinations of what is possible or impossible, or how precisely things work, are Adept- or Master-level effects. Is nuclear fission operating the way it does an Earthly Foundation? That's a Forces 5/Matter 5 effect, there, so by those standards Reality Zones can't cause or prevent that. Creating the Gauntlet in the first place was a Spirit 5 effect, and making it stronger or weaker permanently is a Spirit 4 effect; I'm pretty sure the Consensus can shape how thick the Gauntlet is. Can human belief generate Nodes and Junctures? That's a Prime 5 effect.<br /> <br /> Oh, and one more - changing what's Coincidental or Vulgar in an area?<br /> <br /> That's a Spirit or Dimensional Science 4 effect.<br /> <br /> I'm... pretty sure that the Consensus can do that.<br /> <br /> There are other examples, but... yeah. What constitutes how many dots an Effect requires isn't always magnitude of the change so much as <i>depth</i> and <i>precision</i> of the change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-20-2016, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T15:55:29-07:00","id":973456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=973345#post973345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and I'd be looking askance at the VEs for choosing to make Conventional Space an inhospitable freezing, weightless vacuum</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes it more difficult for hostile aliens to show up. Hell, preventing the Mi Go from riding the ether-winds from Saturn might be enough to justify that being a deliberate choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T17:20:48-07:00","id":973514,"title":"","content":"Bad thing to mix Mythos with WoD (and MI Go live on Pluto, not Saturn).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T17:27:04-07:00","id":973519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=973514#post973514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bad thing to mix Mythos with WoD (and MI Go live on Pluto, not Saturn).</div> </div> </div> </div>WoD itself already mixes Mythos and WoD. What do you think the K'llashaa Nephandi are based on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T18:28:15-07:00","id":973554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=973113#post973113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You just asked what is in the books that you are failing to acknowledge, other than the stuff you are failing to acknowledge. Deal with the stuff on your plate before asking for desert.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don`t have to acknowledge anything that isn`t in the books as default in this forum. If we are going to discuss opinion, state that this is <b>your </b>opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=973113#post973113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of which, I was actually holding off responding to you to see if you were going to ignore this one:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> True to form, you did.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ignored it because I believe it's from Sorcerer Crusade. I don't know this system and I am not discussing it. If you have some evidence about Consensus directly changing geography in M20, then show it, please.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=973113#post973113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But here's the big thing I missed before. Look at where Laptops stop working. It's not in population centers, it's in the distant places of the world with low or no population. Laptops stop working where the Consensus is weak. That means it is the Consensus that makes them work, not the Consensus that stops them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is relative and doesnt make any difference. As I said, I ok with Consensus making things possible/impossible, as vulgar or coincident. I'm definitely <b>not </b>ok with Consensus making earth flat/round or making the universe made of atoms/elements according to people belief.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T19:24:00-07:00","id":973589,"title":"","content":"Are you OK with the atom theory being a Technocratic invention, part of their paradigm rather than an established truth? Because I could see that as a possibility: the only proof we have that the universe is made up of atoms arguably comes from Technocratic instruments. They haven't made the universe's composition be atoms, nor has the Consensus; but that doesn't mean that the universe <i>is</i> made of atoms; only that they <i>say</i> it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T19:48:17-07:00","id":973600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=973554#post973554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ignored it because I believe it's from Sorcerer Crusade. I don't know this system and I am not discussing it. If you have some evidence about Consensus directly changing geography in M20, then show it, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would totally respect your dedication to using only the most recent edition if your only two quotes didn't come from Revised. M20 was written to allow as many play styles as possible, though, so good luck finding a single default.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, Sorcerer's Crusade is just the historical setting for Mage. It's not a different system like Dark Ages is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is relative and doesnt make any difference. As I said, I ok with Consensus making things possible/impossible, as vulgar or coincident. I'm definitely <b>not </b>ok with Consensus making earth flat/round or making the universe made of atoms/elements according to people belief. </div> </div> </div>Revan, I don't care how you play your games, run them however you want. My problem is your insistence that modern physics and an unchanging world are the default, and that anyone who says anything else is taking liberties with the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 09-20-2016, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T21:27:12-07:00","id":973640,"title":"","content":"The atomic theory predates the Technocracy by around two thousand years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T23:38:43-07:00","id":973690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=973640#post973640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The atomic theory predates the Technocracy by around two thousand years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because Demokrit reasoned that there have to be a smallest part of matter does not mean that it is perceivable, just imaginable.<br /> <br /> Shamanism predates the Traditions by ages, likewise High Ritual and Miracle Working and Witchcraft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T02:54:17-07:00","id":973733,"title":"","content":"The Greeks as a whole were... kind of scattershot in their theories about the fundamental composition of the universe. So yes, the idea of the world being made of indivisible grains was first brought up by the ancient Greeks... as was it being made of fire, or water, or numbers, and frankly I would be wholly unsurprised if there was <i>some</i> Greek philosopher <i>somewhere</i> that hypothesized that the world was made entirely of very small bees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T04:45:03-07:00","id":973755,"title":"","content":"In case some people find it useful, here are some of the ways I've seen Mage interpreted over the years. All of these are supported in varying degrees by the books.<br /> <br /> 1) There is no structure to reality. Nothing really exists and the Consensus just makes things happen anyways. The harder the Consensus believes something, the harder it is to change their minds.<br /> <br /> 2) Without a Consensus or some other similar force Reality looks like the Deep Umbra. Consensus creates the structure of the world and things happen because of that structure.<br /> <br /> 3) There is some kind of structure underlying reality, possibly left by the Pure Ones (if they ever existed). Whatever the case, the Consensus can completely override and rewrite that structure.<br /> <br /> 4) There are a few pieces of unchangeable reality that underlay Consensual Reality (mostly for ST benefit). Everything else can technically be rewritten, although much of it won't be.<br /> <br /> 5) There's a whole bunch of rules that can't be changed, but many more rules are just products of the Consensus. The big things can't be changed, but other parts of reality can be completely rewritten.<br /> <br /> 6) There is a complete and defined reality that underlays Consensual Reality. The Consensus doesn't change that structure, but can force things to happen against it.<br /> <br /> 7) There is a large complicated reality underneath Consensual Reality. The Consensus can change the way it manifests to a large degree, but not always in predictable ways.<br /> <br /> 8) Everything is True. Consensual Reality just dictates which True things manifest. Some of you might recognize the main proponent of that one.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's not an exhaustive list, and many people mix two or more of these, but it gives an idea of just what ideas Mage inspires in people. Mage is a game that offers a lot of possibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T05:54:28-07:00","id":973781,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a>, Still, it's not quite part of Mage the Ascension. Also, I am not discussing it as I really don't know it.<br /> <br /> Congratulations, almost all of your points there have absolutely no base in the books. It's your view, so you're free to have it and share it... as yiur personal view.<br /> <br /> To make things clear one last time:<br /> <br /> I didn't said there is one big truth in Mage and that this truth is real physics. I just said that it is natural thst our physics is the default. <br /> <br /> If someone create a thread asking about earth shape, atoms etc.. The right answer is &quot;There is no answer for this, you can make as you want as a ST&quot;.<br /> &quot;there are atoms, the earth is round, etc.&quot; is probably wrong as nowhere in the book it is said that it's the truth, other than the game taking place in a universe like our. But saying &quot;earth was flat then round and universe is made of elements&quot; is complety wrong, as this is a ST call and there is NO evidence of such in the book. It is as wrong as saying the universe is made of ice cream.<br /> <br /> I hope you finally understand, I'm tired of posting the same things over and over.<br /> <br /> Dataweaver, as others pointed we don't know for sure if the atom theory was created by the Technocracy<br /> Considering it was, yes, I'm ok with the universe not being made of atoms. If I were to ST a game it definitely would be made of atoms, though. What I'm not ok is saying that this is not the &quot;default&quot; assumption we should take when discussing in this forum. <br /> It's like someone asks in a thread how much Forces is meeded to vibrate the atoms around someone to create heat and you say that the universe is not made of atoms, so he can't do that. Unless he tells us his mage doesn't believe in atoms, we assume he universe is made and he can do it with Forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T05:57:20-07:00","id":973784,"title":"","content":"it's actually perfectly coincidental to set someone on fire by just glancing at them. Ever heard of spontaneous combustion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:58:12-07:00","id":973828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=973781#post973781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Congratulations, almost all of your points there have absolutely no base in the books. It's your view, so you're free to have it and share it... as yiur personal view.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I were to ST a game it definitely would be made of atoms, though. What I'm not ok is saying that this is not the &quot;default&quot; assumption we should take when discussing in this forum. </div> </div> </div>This, this right here, is why there is such an issue. Those weren't points, they were interpretations of the game, and they weren't even all mine. And you just dismissed them. Worse you are trying to tell us how we are allowed to discuss Mage on the Mage forums. What the hell?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If someone create a thread asking about earth shape, atoms etc.. The right answer is &quot;There is no answer for this, you can make as you want as a ST&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Broadly correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;there are atoms, the earth is round, etc.&quot; is probably wrong as nowhere in the book it is said that it's the truth, other than the game taking place in a universe like our. </div> </div> </div>Also correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But saying &quot;earth was flat then round and universe is made of elements&quot; is complety wrong, as this is a ST call and there is NO evidence of such in the book. It is as wrong as saying the universe is made of ice cream. </div> </div> </div>But using those as an example of what is open in Mage games is entirely reasonable. If you want to eliminate those possibilities from your game it is easy enough to do by painting them as one of the Earthly Foundations or Cosmological Constants. Those are specifically in the books. You don't need to strictly define a default play style.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's like someone asks in a thread how much Forces is meeded to vibrate the atoms around someone to create heat and you say that the universe is not made of atoms, so he can't do that. Unless he tells us his mage doesn't believe in atoms, we assume he universe is made and he can do it with Forces. </div> </div> </div>Why did you even bring this up? Which view of Mage does this not work in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:59:04-07:00","id":973829,"title":"","content":"Yes, I heard of it plus it happens almost always when the torch to be is alone...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=973781#post973781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, Still, it's not quite part of Mage the Ascension. Also, I am not discussing it as I really don't know it.<br /> <br /> Congratulations, almost all of your points there have absolutely no base in the books. It's your view, so you're free to have it and share it... as yiur personal view.<br /> <br /> To make things clear one last time:<br /> <br /> I didn't said there is one big truth in Mage and that this truth is real physics. I just said that it is natural thst our physics is the default. <br /> <br /> If someone create a thread asking about earth shape, atoms etc.. The right answer is &amp;quot;There is no answer for this, you can make as you want as a ST&amp;quot;.<br /> &amp;quot;there are atoms, the earth is round, etc.&amp;quot; is probably wrong as nowhere in the book it is said that it's the truth, other than the game taking place in a universe like our. But saying &amp;quot;earth was flat then round and universe is made of elements&amp;quot; is complety wrong, as this is a ST call and there is NO evidence of such in the book. It is as wrong as saying the universe is made of ice cream.<br /> <br /> I hope you finally understand, I'm tired of posting the same things over and over.<br /> <br /> Dataweaver, as others pointed we don't know for sure if the atom theory was created by the Technocracy<br /> Considering it was, yes, I'm ok with the universe not being made of atoms. If I were to ST a game it definitely would be made of atoms, though. What I'm not ok is saying that this is not the &amp;quot;default&amp;quot; assumption we should take when discussing in this forum. <br /> It's like someone asks in a thread how much Forces is meeded to vibrate the atoms around someone to create heat and you say that the universe is not made of atoms, so he can't do that. Unless he tells us his mage doesn't believe in atoms, we assume he universe is made and he can do it with Forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regardless of the Reality of atoms, every mage believing in atoms can work with them.<br /> The point is that, to a mage, it matters not if Reality conforms to his believe.<br /> He can make reality bend to his will","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12022,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","user":"Nonsense","date":". 09-21-2016, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T08:10:30-07:00","id":973861,"title":"","content":"Well, I think that it is more that Mages can make reality bend to their will up to the limit allowed by their paradigm. Technocratic Archmages can build devices that levitate entire aircraft carriers, but they cannot simply levitate grains of sand by pointing their fingers because it is against their paradigm. As for spontaneous human combustion, the Consensus does not accept it because there have been no scientifically verified examples of spontaneous human combustion (it is, as yet, simply urban myth). The reports of humans achieving temperatures of 2000 C are absurd and, quite frankly unnecessary, as human bodies will comfortably burn at 250 C (if spontaneous human combustion was real, the incidences would have probably just resulted in an oily fire, rather than the clean fire that is claimed, as humans do not burn clean unless they have been mummified).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T08:30:23-07:00","id":973869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=973784#post973784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> it's actually perfectly coincidental to set someone on fire by just glancing at them. Ever heard of spontaneous combustion?</div> </div> </div> </div>These cases are Vulgar attacks with Forces, obviously.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T18:11:40-07:00","id":974146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=973828#post973828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This, this right here, is why there is such an issue. Those weren't points, they were interpretations of the game, and they weren't even all mine. And you just dismissed them. Worse you are trying to tell us how we are allowed to discuss Mage on the Mage forums. What the hell?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't adopt some view as the default you would need an entire background data of the ST table to begin posting. Like, if the ST of OP in the example consider an universe made of atoms, the flat or round earth, etc.<br /> <br /> Actually, you already consider our universe as default, since I doubt you always ask about OP table universe every time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=973828#post973828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But using those as an example of what is open in Mage games is entirely reasonable. If you want to eliminate those possibilities from your game it is easy enough to do by painting them as one of the Earthly Foundations or Cosmological Constants. Those are specifically in the books. You don't need to strictly define a default play style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know if I get it. Being reasonable is different of being true.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=973828#post973828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why did you even bring this up? Which view of Mage does this not work in?</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. So would you adapt the player effect to the reality you have in your game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars