t973828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But using those as an example of what is open in Mage games is entirely reasonable. If you want to eliminate those possibilities from your game it is easy enough to do by painting them as one of the Earthly Foundations or Cosmological Constants. Those are specifically in the books. You don't need to strictly define a default play style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know if I get it. Being reasonable is different of being true.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=973828#post973828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why did you even bring this up? Which view of Mage does this not work in?</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. So would you adapt the player effect to the reality you have in your game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T19:45:50-07:00","id":974192,"title":"","content":"Of course the world is made of atoms now. Though, you don't need Forces to vibrate them and cause heat, that's a Consensual action. You don't even need Numina. Just like, rub your hands together or something.<br /> <br /> Rubbing your hands together is very powerful and ancient magic for warming oneself, you see.<br /> <br /> Those were a useful invention, atoms, made it really easy to do otherwise-complicated material procedures once they were implemented. Heck, nowadays we can even modify those atoms since we managed to introduce <i>even smaller</i> atoms! It's <i>amazing</i>. Especially the part where they don't have a definite location, makes the Voidcast and other teleportation between fixed regions more efficient as an instantaneous thing. Heck, it even makes it easier to use wormhole travel methods once you've figured out how QM and General Relativity mesh.<br /> <br /> The Masses just <i>eat this shit up</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":".  Terminology fix 09-22-2016, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T20:55:46-07:00","id":974215,"title":"","content":"Hm, you really do not understand physics, do you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T23:05:30-07:00","id":974252,"title":"","content":"Oh, oh this is perfect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T02:54:02-07:00","id":974309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=974215#post974215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, you really do not understand physics, do you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm only <i>actually</i> trained as a computer scientist, but I have a general university-level science education. I'd like to think I have a <i>basic</i> grasp of how physics works in our universe, and when it goes past that I know a career physicist or two to consult. I'm not sure how my understanding of real-world physics is pertinent to the topic though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T05:41:54-07:00","id":974349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=974147#post974147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't adopt some view as the default you would need an entire background data of the ST table to begin posting. Like, if the ST of OP in the example consider an universe made of atoms, the flat or round earth, etc.<br /> <br /> Actually, you already consider our universe as default, since I doubt you always ask about OP table universe every time.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some some things we can generally agree are true, yes, but Mage is not written specifically enough to justify the level of detail you are looking for. We can say that modern Mage world at least looks like our own, but is that because it is, or because it is forced to be, or because it isn't but it is forced to behave as if it is? All of those are consistent with what is written to a lesser or greater degree.<br /> <br /> Indeed we don't even need to define it more narrowly than that to handle the OP's questions. All we need to know is what the Consensus believes can happen in those cases and how tightly it locks it down. Whether that belief actually forces reality into a shape or just appears to is immaterial in this case.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't know if I get it. Being reasonable is different of being true. </div> </div> </div>We are talking about interpretations of a fictional universe, truth doesn't enter into it. Given that this is Mage, that might even be by design. The only thing we can do is see if our ideas are consistent with what is written.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see. So would you adapt the player effect to the reality you have in your game? </div> </div> </div>Yes. I suspect you do too. The Traditions frequently use principles that just don't exist in our world, be they mountains that connect to every location, Orgone energy, or a secret 'source code' of reality. It doesn't matter, they can still force their Will on the world and what has to happen to make it work happens. It would work the same way for Hypertech in a Mythic world.<br /> <br /> The only two styles I've ever seen that don't have to adapt anything are 'Nothing is True' and 'Everything is True.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 09-22-2016, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T05:44:21-07:00","id":974350,"title":"","content":"Strange, I would think that a computer scientist would know the difference between entanglement and tunneling. I will explain though why your example did not work. Entanglement is a form of quantum communication between two related particles so, if a scientific paradigm was used, it would allow for instantaneous or interdimentional communication (not travel). Tunneling is a form of quantum teleportation that occurs when a particle encounters a barrier with a thickness less than its wavelength so, if a scientific paradigm was used, it would be used to justify instantaneous or interdimentional travel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T05:52:05-07:00","id":974354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=974350#post974350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strange, I would think that a computer scientist would know the difference between entanglement and tunneling. I will explain though why your example did not work. Entanglement is a form of quantum communication between two related particles so, if a scientific paradigm was used, it would allow for instantaneous or interdimentional communication (not travel). Tunneling is a form of quantum teleportation that occurs when a particle encounters a barrier with a thickness less than its wavelength so, if a scientific paradigm was used, it would be used to justify instantaneous or interdimentional travel.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, you could make a teleporter that works by just sending the data for how to rebuild the teleportee on the other side. If you have enough matter, sometimes communication is all you need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T06:05:45-07:00","id":974359,"title":"","content":"No one in the Technocracy is going to create a Star Trek teleporter, it violates the scientific paradigm too much. The required data would be around a trillion TB or so and, since the best transfer speeds are around 10 GB per second, it would be faster to walk to the desired location. In addition, the Avatar stays with the first body, so the resulting clone would just be an Extraordinary Citizen rather than a Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T06:10:06-07:00","id":974361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=974354#post974354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand, you could make a teleporter that works by just sending the data for how to rebuild the teleportee on the other side. If you have enough matter, sometimes communication is all you need.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't be <i>the person who was sent by the teleporter</i>!<br /> (Unless you add Mind to transfer their mind, of course. Or perhaps Spirit for the soul. While keeping them intact.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-22-2016, 09:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T06:39:16-07:00","id":974373,"title":"","content":"@Quamtumboost @Ramnesis<br /> <br /> Let me explain what is my problem even better.<br /> <br /> My thought on Mage reality is that there is only one in game reality. A pencil cannot be made of atoms and elements. The earth cannot be flat and round. Diseases cannot be caused by virus and demons (altought demons could indlict disease, but through viruses, i don't know).<br /> <br /> So, while reality is completely malleable, it doesn't mean that it is more than one. The thing is, the purple paradigm is true, this is repeated over and over in the books. And that is why a mage rubbing his hand can heal someone as a mage using antibiotics. <br /> <br /> While there are atoms and viruses, reality let anyone who knows how to and Wills, to change it, change it.<br /> Then, the mage that thinks that he is healing the demons of a ill person, is in fact forcing his Will upon reality to destroy the virus inside him.<br /> <br /> Quantumboost, your post is the belief of a mage and it doesn't mean it is true. I guess the majority of ST have their games following our real physics, which doesn't mean that the mages that don't believe in it can't cast spells with other instruments. It's their Will that changes reality, afterall","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 09-22-2016, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T07:50:14-07:00","id":974412,"title":"","content":"Two things:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=974359#post974359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one in the Technocracy is going to create a Star Trek teleporter, it violates the scientific paradigm too much. The required data would be around a trillion TB or so and, since the best transfer speeds are around 10 GB per second, it would be faster to walk to the desired location. In addition, the Avatar stays with the first body, so the resulting clone would just be an Extraordinary Citizen rather than a Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>The best transfer speeds according to what exactly? Sleeper tech? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The Technocratic Union has credit-card hologram-interface computers, and smartphones that get satellite connections inside an underground bunker, so going by mundane transfer speeds isn't the wisest decision - It's why it's Hypertech in the first place, instead of mundane tech.<br /> <br /> Additionally, regarding the avatar..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=974361#post974361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wouldn't be <i>the person who was sent by the teleporter</i>!<br /> (Unless you add Mind to transfer their mind, of course. Or perhaps Spirit for the soul. While keeping them intact.)</div> </div> </div> </div>^-- This would maaaybe solve the issue regarding the Avatar, although I would say that, yes, you need a combination of Spirit/Prime to transfer it. It might just work, given that the mind gets transferred, or at least there is an identical mind to attach to.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, regarding scientific paradigms, a little tale:<br /> It would perfectly fit an '<i>Everything is Data</i>' paradigm.<br /> The kicker is.. RL example...I *know* transhumanist flavored 'Everything is data' people. I had the exact argument with them regarding Star Trek teleporters: &quot;<i>Star trek teleporters kill the original, what's left it's a clone, not you!</i>&quot;<br /> The same regarding the whole '<i>Download our minds into computers for immortality</i>' shtick. I went &quot;<i>It's not a transfer, it's just a copy, the real you is still outside the computer and will die as usual!</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Their reply pretty much was &quot;<i>What difference does it make? The resulting mind/person is for all intents and purposes me, all the data on a physical level is me. All the data in the computer would be the same. The original me dieing wouldn't matter as the result would virtually be the same me again.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> So yeah. There are people right now like that who *are* that...scientifically pragmatic. The data is the same, ergo the end result would be them again for all intents and purposes. A copy, but a copy that is in all aspects them nontheless, so it doesn't matter if the original dies. 'Nothing is lost' in their mindset, concerning the rest of the world.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be hard to imagine some Technocrats having no problem with the very idea.<br /> <br /> I get where they are coming from, but I reeeally can't subscribe to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-23-2016, 03:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T08:42:59-07:00","id":974432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=974373#post974373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Quamtumboost @Ramnesis<br /> <br /> Let me explain what is my problem even better.<br /> <br /> My thought on Mage reality is that there is only one in game reality. A pencil cannot be made of atoms and elements. The earth cannot be flat and round. Diseases cannot be caused by virus and demons (altought demons could indlict disease, but through viruses, i don't know).<br /> <br /> So, while reality is completely malleable, it doesn't mean that it is more than one. The thing is, the purple paradigm is true, this is repeated over and over in the books. And that is why a mage rubbing his hand can heal someone as a mage using antibiotics.<br /> <br /> While there are atoms and viruses, reality let anyone who knows how to and Wills, to change it, change it.<br /> Then, the mage that thinks that he is healing the demons of a ill person, is in fact forcing his Will upon reality to destroy the virus inside him.<br /> <br /> Quantumboost, your post is the belief of a mage and it doesn't mean it is true. I guess the majority of ST have their games following our real physics, which doesn't mean that the mages that don't believe in it can't cast spells with other instruments. It's their Will that changes reality, afterall</div> </div> </div> </div>I get where you are coming from, and it is certainly a way of viewing Mage. It just isn't the only way. I don't think you can even say it is the majority view, nor would it matter if you could. There are a lot of different opinions on what Mage means and how it is played, and even claims you'd think are uncontroversial will face criticism from some quarters (as you've actually reminded me of recently).. Honestly, that's half the fun of being on these forums, the constant comparing and contrasting of different viewpoints and testing to see what works.<br /> <br /> I think I will add one more quote here, which is possibly one of the better things I read in M20. It's not something that proves you wrong or anything, it just gives a little insight into some of the thought's behind Mage:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20, pg 617</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Change the Game and Change Your World<br /> The choice between those options belongs to each individual group and Storyteller. Mage, however, has always been dedicated to the idea of transformation. The very first tagline for Mage \u2013 one that was never actually published and which appeared only on the in-house drafts created by the original authors \u2013 was \u201cA Storytelling game of changing reality.\u201d And although that sentiment lacks the immediacy of Mage\u2019s other taglines, the idea that you CAN change the world is an essential element of the game.<br /> As Uncle Al said, do what you Will.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T10:27:13-07:00","id":974501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=974350#post974350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strange, I would think that a computer scientist would know the difference between entanglement and tunneling. I will explain though why your example did not work. Entanglement is a form of quantum communication between two related particles so, if a scientific paradigm was used, it would allow for instantaneous or interdimentional communication (not travel). Tunneling is a form of quantum teleportation that occurs when a particle encounters a barrier with a thickness less than its wavelength so, if a scientific paradigm was used, it would be used to justify instantaneous or interdimentional travel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Yeah, made a minor terminology mistake there. I tend to view them as related phenomena and don't really <i>use</i> that level of (very not basic) physics outside of Mage games very often.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=974359#post974359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one in the Technocracy is going to create a Star Trek teleporter, it violates the scientific paradigm too much. The required data would be around a trillion TB or so and, since the best transfer speeds are around 10 GB per second, it would be faster to walk to the desired location. In addition, the Avatar stays with the first body, so the resulting clone would just be an Extraordinary Citizen rather than a Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the Progenitors would totally do that. Iteration X and the Virtual Adepts too. Transform the mindstate (<i>including the Avatar</i>, which they believe is an aspect of the mind) into an information stream, transmit it through hypertech high-density transfer mechanisms, then 'install' it on a cloned body or other construct on the other side. Or just upload it to the Digital Web.<br /> <br /> Granted, they might or might not use QE, particle-stream information transfer like Eclipse Phase-style egocasting is also a plausible means.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, that's just an Mind 5/Correspondence 2-5 (the Digital Web's existence is amazing for reducing the Corr requirements here) Untether effect coupled with Apportation and a Possession on the other side. Their paradigm and the use of Untether takes care of Avatar-related matters.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=974373#post974373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quantumboost, your post is the belief of a mage and it doesn't mean it is true. I guess the majority of ST have their games following our real physics, which doesn't mean that the mages that don't believe in it can't cast spells with other instruments. It's their Will that changes reality, afterall</div> </div> </div> </div>That's nice.<br /> <br /> I've read the back-and-forth with Ramnesis, though, so I'm not going to fall into that trap.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=974412#post974412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The kicker is.. RL example...I *know* transhumanist flavored 'Everything is data' people. I had the exact argument with them regarding Star Trek teleporters: &quot;<i>Star trek teleporters kill the original, what's left it's a clone, not you!</i>&quot;<br /> The same regarding the whole '<i>Download our minds into computers for immortality</i>' shtick. I went &quot;<i>It's not a transfer, it's just a copy, the real you is still outside the computer and will die as usual!</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Their reply pretty much was &quot;<i>What difference does it make? The resulting mind/person is for all intents and purposes me, all the data on a physical level is me. All the data in the computer would be the same. The original me dieing wouldn't matter as the result would virtually be the same me again.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> So yeah. There are people right now like that who *are* that...scientifically pragmatic. The data is the same, ergo the end result would be them again for all intents and purposes. A copy, but a copy that is in all aspects them nontheless, so it doesn't matter if the original dies. 'Nothing is lost' in their mindset, concerning the rest of the world.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be hard to imagine some Technocrats having no problem with the very idea.<br /> <br /> I get where they are coming from, but I reeeally can't subscribe to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's essentially a question of how you view identity. Effectively, if you believe that identity is some sort of singular continuity stream or a fundamental anchor of existence (hi there Exalted!) then teleporting like that can't possibly work. If you believe that identity is predicated solely on continuity of some aspects of your mind's pattern, then teleporting like that would obviously work if it's high-fidelity enough.<br /> <br /> There's a variety of other possible positions on the identity issue, with natural implications for the resulting position on teh teleprots.<br /> <br /> There are also interesting implications from how individual fundamental particles don't seem to have individual identities.<br /> <br /> If you subscribe to something akin to the latter position, teleporting is just a matter of temporarily displacing the youness in your mindstate in space a bit, kind of like how falling asleep might displace it in time a bit. Of course, this is also not terribly compatible with the notion of a unique soul which is inherently distinct from everyone else's (perhaps not wibbly-wobbly indistinct souls), though Exalted-style biomotonic replicants bring up the additional question of how much the soul matters overall.<br /> <br /> Of course, the best solution is to surpass the notion of location in order to put your mind and spirit in multiple bodies at once. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-22-2016, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T10:38:28-07:00","id":974514,"title":"","content":"Destroying the spirit of a disease does, in fact, cause the disease to clear up in the physical world, mage or no mage.<br /> <br /> The theme of this thread is bad examples.<br /> <br /> (although it doesn't necessarily work the other way around!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":1653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","user":"Five Eyes","date":". 09-22-2016, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T14:16:33-07:00","id":974659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=974412#post974412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best transfer speeds according to what exactly? Sleeper tech? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The technocratic Union has credit-card hologram-interface computers, and smartphones that get sattelite connections inside an underground bunker, so going by mundane transfer speeds isn't the wisest decision - It's why it's Hypertech in the first place, instead of mundane tech.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Given that the ADEI implants that Iterators love so much, when combined with an implant radio allow you to instantly download enough information to be treated as having a 4 ranks in a skill, talent, or knowledge you wouldn't otherwise have....<br /> <br /> I'd say they've got some pretty decent transfer speeds. Given 4 ranks in &quot;Physics&quot; is just below peak human possibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T15:10:55-07:00","id":974692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=974659#post974659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Given that the ADEI implants that Iterators love so much, when combined with an implant radio allow you to instantly download enough information to be treated as having a 4 ranks in a skill, talent, or knowledge you wouldn't otherwise have....<br /> <br /> I'd say they've got some pretty decent transfer speeds. Given 4 ranks in &quot;Physics&quot; is just below peak human possibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>so like 4G LTE? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T01:17:24-07:00","id":982594,"title":"","content":"I knew I would eventually find it!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20020424225627/http://www.nada.kth.se/~asa/Mage/democracy.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20020424225627im_/http:/www.nada.kth.se/~asa/bilder/r_up.gif\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20020424225627/http://www.nada.kth.se/~asa/Mage/democracy.html\" target=\"_blank\"> A Democratic Paradigm </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20020424225627/http://www.nada.kth.se/~asa/Mage/democracy.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://web.archive.org/web/20020424225627/http://www.nada.kth.se/~asa/Mage/democracy.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T09:05:03-07:00","id":985453,"title":"","content":"I lean towards Ramnesis view on things. There is no such thing as objectivity in mage. Everything is subjective and when subjectivity of many sleeper aligns it appears like objectivity. <br /> <br /> The shape of the earth doesn't matter, what you see does. The earth might have been flat but it didn't really matter truly. A sudden revelation by one person doesn't change anything but the perception of the masses takes time and effort to change. That's the whole point of mage. Creating something from nothing violates physics but certain regions might allow it if the people there believe you're a shaman and shamans can do such things. coincidental vs vulgar is fighting against the sleeper view of reality in your vicinity (or against opposing views in horizon realms where reality is ruled by a specific paradigm). The existence or absence of atoms doesn't matter. They don't necessarily need to exist for an effect to take place. If thats how the consensual reality wants to explain it sure, and that'll makes anything working without atoms more difficult but not impossible for a willworker who break the rules.<br /> <br /> The world -seems- like ours. Because the existing paradigm of the sleepers leans toward the technocrat point of view. They've been working exhaustively to slowly introduce higher orders of technology and scientific paradigm over a century or more. <br /> <br /> ((If it seems a bit rambling I'm sorry, posting from phone and it makes it exceedingly difficult to review my post and make edits.))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T20:46:38-07:00","id":985923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrostFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=985453#post985453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I lean towards Ramnesis view on things. There is no such thing as objectivity in mage. Everything is subjective and when subjectivity of many sleeper aligns it appears like objectivity.</div> </div> </div> </div>If everything is subjective, then the Technocracy is objectively wrong. And yes, that's a paradox.<br /> <br /> Put another way: if everything is subjective \u2014 and in particular, defined by the will of the majority \u2014 then why doesn't reality in <b>Mage</b> conform to popular opinion? Want to get rid of Climate Change? Convince the majority of the Sleepers that it doesn't exist, and it doesn't. Think that the Holocaust was a wretched blight on human history? Convince everyone to become Holocaust deniers, and the Holocaust never happened. Anything you don't like about reality can be made to go away if you can just get enough people to deny that it exists. As long as there's no truth beyond majority opinion, that's an entirely rational response to anything you don't like about reality: spread enough Denial around, and you can eradicate it.<br /> <br /> That's why I say that while the Consensus can <i>influence</i> reality, it's a mistake to say that it <i>defines</i> reality. There are Earthly Foundations, Cosmological Constants, Historical Inertia, the Will of the Godhead; whatever else you want to call it, there are things that are true even when the Consensus says they're not, and vice versa. Vampires and werewolves and ghosts exist whether the Masses believe in them or not. The truth about Climate Change doesn't depend on whether people think it's real. The tragedies of human history still happened even if expunged from the history books. There are limits to how much the Consensus can change things, and the Consensus <i>can</i> be out of step with what's really true.<br /> <br /> Or else Denial becomes a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-12-2016, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T05:20:09-07:00","id":986060,"title":"","content":"Yes, it is one of the primary weaknesses of any subjective philosophy. It eventually devolves to a narcissist fantasy because you can set reality by wishing really, really hard. It just works out better, from a philosophical point of view, if all Mages are lunatics whose perceptions are altered by their Avatars to fit their paradigms (Marauders have just stumbled on the ability to externality their lunacy).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T05:52:37-07:00","id":986074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=985923#post985923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If everything is subjective, then the Technocracy is objectively wrong. And yes, that's a paradox.<br /> <br /> Put another way: if everything is subjective \u2014 and in particular, defined by the will of the majority \u2014 then why doesn't reality in <b>Mage</b> conform to popular opinion? Want to get rid of Climate Change? Convince the majority of the Sleepers that it doesn't exist, and it doesn't. Think that the Holocaust was a wretched blight on human history? Convince everyone to become Holocaust deniers, and the Holocaust never happened. Anything you don't like about reality can be made to go away if you can just get enough people to deny that it exists. As long as there's no truth beyond majority opinion, that's an entirely rational response to anything you don't like about reality: spread enough Denial around, and you can eradicate it.<br /> <br /> That's why I say that while the Consensus can <i>influence</i> reality, it's a mistake to say that it <i>defines</i> reality. There are Earthly Foundations, Cosmological Constants, Historical Inertia, the Will of the Godhead; whatever else you want to call it, there are things that are true even when the Consensus says they're not, and vice versa. Vampires and werewolves and ghosts exist whether the Masses believe in them or not. The truth about Climate Change doesn't depend on whether people think it's real. The tragedies of human history still happened even if expunged from the history books. There are limits to how much the Consensus can change things, and the Consensus <i>can</i> be out of step with what's really true.<br /> <br /> Or else Denial becomes a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how it makes the Technocracy objectively wrong so you'll have to elaborate on that for me.<br /> <br /> As for the rest...Yes. You can manipulate the majority to reverse climate change by introducing cleaner tech or purifying rituals (depending on your paradigm). Changing the structure of reality doesn't change its past structure it just changes how it develops in the future.<br /> <br /> You're correct in saying that from an objective standpoint denying the holocaust won't miraculously change reality to a state in which it didn't happen. But it is possible to effectively deny the holocaust by expunging the records and letting it fade from memory. Then it's effectively as if it never happened but that's incredibly difficult and frankly what's the point. The technocracy doesn't need to deny history, just needs to paint it as a time of ignorance to the true workings of the universe (according to their paradigm) and no one living remembers that time so all the presented evidence must be true. <br /> <br /> But really...most people don't care beyond their immediate needs. It doesn't matter how reality functions as long as it continues to do so and they can lead their lives day by day. Most people think about their day to day needs, not about higher orders of thought and the workings of the universe (especially in the world of darkness where the masses are more gullible, guideable, and ignorant).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2818,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","user":"FrostFox","date":". 10-12-2016, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T06:28:56-07:00","id":986091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=985923#post985923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If everything is subjective, then the Technocracy is objectively wrong. And yes, that's a paradox.<br /> <br /> Put another way: if everything is subjective \u2014 and in particular, defined by the will of the majority \u2014 then why doesn't reality in <b>Mage</b> conform to popular opinion? Want to get rid of Climate Change? Convince the majority of the Sleepers that it doesn't exist, and it doesn't. Think that the Holocaust was a wretched blight on human history? Convince everyone to become Holocaust deniers, and the Holocaust never happened. Anything you don't like about reality can be made to go away if you can just get enough people to deny that it exists. As long as there's no truth beyond majority opinion, that's an entirely rational response to anything you don't like about reality: spread enough Denial around, and you can eradicate it.<br /> <br /> That's why I say that while the Consensus can <i>influence</i> reality, it's a mistake to say that it <i>defines</i> reality. There are Earthly Foundations, Cosmological Constants, Historical Inertia, the Will of the Godhead; whatever else you want to call it, there are things that are true even when the Consensus says they're not, and vice versa. Vampires and werewolves and ghosts exist whether the Masses believe in them or not. The truth about Climate Change doesn't depend on whether people think it's real. The tragedies of human history still happened even if expunged from the history books. There are limits to how much the Consensus can change things, and the Consensus <i>can</i> be out of step with what's really true.<br /> <br /> Or else Denial becomes a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>All things are subjective, but some are more subjective than others.<br /> <br /> Even without appealing to some kind of outside constant it is reasonable, and indeed likely, that some things would be much harder to change. Gravity, momentum, oxygen, these are all things that every person on the planet has been dealing with from before they could even speak. Their expectations are well and truly set. It is entirely possible to depict Earthly Foundations and Historical Inertia as products of the consensus. Mythic Threads too, if we allow for it to be more complicated than simple majority rule.<br /> <br /> Now there are two things I put outside the reach of Consensual Reality. The first is Consensual Reality itself. People don't believe they can alter reality with belief, so if they could take that power away from themselves, they would have by now. They also can't change who affects the Consensus, or write them out of existence. The second is morality. Not in the sense that morality is objective, but in the sense that mages should never know if it is or not. The question of whether might makes right is more powerful if you can't answer it for certain.<br /> <br /> The door is wide open for other constants, of course, but it is surprising how far you can get with just those two. The revisionist history angle, for instance, doesn't come up. The Consensus can no more make the holocaust disappear than it can make, say, Mother Theresa into an axe murderer. Changing the past would involve the Consensus writing people out of the Consensus or overriding their will.<br /> <br /> And yes, there will still be some oddities. Sometimes a consensual reality works in counterintuitive or unpleasant ways, but that doesn't mean something has gone wrong. Mage is a game where quack remedies like blood letting and mercury used to work; where we can root for the crazy wizard over the modern scientist. Things we would decry in this world can be positive courses of action in game. There are ways of handling Climate change so that it resists change, it might be a widespread paradox or a hypernarrative. But if convincing the populace that Climate Change isn't happening makes it stops, that also works. Mage isn't our world, it's supposed to be stranger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 10-12-2016, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T08:31:11-07:00","id":986151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrostFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=986074#post986074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how it makes the Technocracy objectively wrong so you'll have to elaborate on that for me.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Technocracy's stance is that there <i>are</i> fundamental, objective truths that remain true regardless of what people believe. (Caveat: the NWO is the exception to this, with their 1984ish \u201creality is whatever the State says it is\u201d view. But they're the exception, with every other Convention \u2014 even the Syndicate \u2014 toeing the line about fundamental truths underlying reality.)<br /> <br /> If reality truly is entirely subjective (key word: \u201centirely\u201d), then the Technocratic position that it <i>isn't</i> entirely subjective is fundamentally wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrostFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=986074#post986074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the rest...Yes. You can manipulate the majority to reverse climate change by introducing cleaner tech or purifying rituals (depending on your paradigm).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what I'm saying. I'm saying that if reality truly is defined by the Consensus, you should be able to get rid of Climate Change <i>strictly by means of a propaganda campaign that convinces the Masses that it doesn't exist.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrostFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=986074#post986074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changing the structure of reality doesn't change its past structure it just changes how it develops in the future. You're correct in saying that from an objective standpoint denying the holocaust won't miraculously change reality to a state in which it didn't happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what I'm saying, either. Time Magick is a thing, which means that the Consensus <i>can</i> alter the past. And barring something like Historical Inertia (which is basically saying \u201cthe past is objectively true, and the Consensus can be wrong about it\u201d), a truly subjective reality defined entirely by the Consensus is one where the past can literally be rewritten by convincing enough people that it was different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=986091#post986091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All things are subjective, but some are more subjective than others.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new Roman\">\u201cAll animals are equal; but some are more equal than others.\u201d \u2014 <i>Animal Farm</i></span></div>Right here, you're tacitly admitting that reality <i>isn't</i> entirely subjective, and that it's possible for there to be a disconnect between the Consensus and Reality \u2014 that is, it's possible for the Consensus to be wrong. Which is what I'm saying. I'm not arguing that the Consensus doesn't <i>influence</i> reality in the world of <b>Mage</b> or that reality doesn't have subjective elements to it; it obviously does, and the Traditions are not wrong point out that belief can change reality. But they <i>are</i> wrong to the extent that they say that reality is entirely a product of the Consensus except when overruled by Enlightened Will. Likewise, the Technocracy isn't wrong to point out that there <i>are</i> things that don't depend on the Consensus to exist; and it may even be right that Technocratic Reality Zones are closer to the default reality that would exist if Willworking (including the collective Willworking of the Consensus) wasn't a factor. It <i>is</i> wrong, and blatantly so, to the extent that it argues that Superstitionists don't have real power and are delusional. The truth of the matter is that reality is neither entirely subjective nor entirely objective; rather, it exists as an uneasy mix of the two.<br /> <br /> And as I've said before, Reality Zone don't define reality; they define the line between Vulgar and Coincidental Magick, what the local Resonance/Synergy is, and <i>possibly</i> what Mythic Threads work. There's nothing in the Reality Zones section that indicates that they affect anything other than Awakened Magick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=986091#post986091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even without appealing to some kind of outside constant it is reasonable, and indeed likely, that some things would be much harder to change. Gravity, momentum, oxygen, these are all things that every person on the planet has been dealing with from before they could even speak. Their expectations are well and truly set. It is entirely possible to depict Earthly Foundations and Historical Inertia as products of the consensus. Mythic Threads too, if we allow for it to be more complicated than simple majority rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>That last caveat is key. Also key is the question of who gets to vote. <b>Mage</b> posits the notion that beings with Avatars have the ability to Willwork, and that beings without Avatars don't. And with the possible exception of the Celestial Chorus' Pure Ones and the Taft\u00e2ni's Djinn, <b>Mage</b> further posits that only humans have Avatars. That means that vampires, werewolves, spirits, and ghosts don't get a vote in the Consensus. Sure, you could argue that there are entities with Avatar-like reality-warping abilities who serve as \u201csponsors\u201d for these beings otherwise have no say in the Consensus; but as soon as you say that, you're redefining what the Consensus is generally understood to mean: it's longer the collective Willworking of humanity's Sleeper population, but rather it's that plus the X-factor of \u201cthe Will of God\u201d or whatever term you wish to apply to the inhuman entities who cause reality to frequently deviate from what the collective beliefs of humanity say it is. And since this X-factor is essentially unknowable, \u201cthe Will of God\u201d is largely indistinguishable from \u201cCosmological Constants\u201d. Do spirits exist as they do because the Triat believes in them, or is it because they're an intrinsic part of reality that can't be expunged by human disbelief (as opposed to the Bygones)? Who knows? What we <i>do</i> know is that spirits aren't subject to the \u201cI don't believe in fairies\u201d phenomenon the way that dragons and unicorns are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=986091#post986091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now there are two things I put outside the reach of Consensual Reality. The first, is Consensual Reality itself. People don't believe they can alter reality with belief, so if they could take that power away from themselves, they would have by now. They also can't change who affects the Consensus, or write them out of existence. The second is morality. Not in the sense that morality is objective, but in the sense that mages should never know if it is or not. The question of whether might makes right is more powerful if you can't answer it for certain.<br /> <br /> The door is wide open for other constants, of course, but it is surprising how far you can get with just those two. The revisionist history angle, for instance, doesn't come up. The Consensus can no more make the holocaust disappear than it can make, say, Mother Theresa into an axe murderer. Changing the past would involve the Consensus writing people out of the Consensus or overriding their will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that the current population of the world dwarfs the entire accumulated population of the world from the dawn of time to, what, the 19th century? you again need something more involved than \u201cmajority rules\u201d to keep the present Consensus from overriding the past. Admittedly, the Holocaust is more recent than that; but then, it wasn't until the end of WWII that it became public knowledge; so the population that you need to override to get rid of it is limited to a little more than the past seven decades of humanity. A tough hurdle, but not necessarily an insurmountable one if you can extend the population explosion (say, by colonizing Space). The point is that you need something more involved than \u201creality is subjective\u201d to keep the promotion of Holocaust Denial from being a viable tactic for retroactively eliminating the Holocaust.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=986091#post986091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, there will still be some oddities. Sometimes a consensual reality works in counterintuitive or unpleasant ways, but that doesn't mean something has gone wrong. Mage is a game where quack remedies like blood letting and mercury used to work; where we can root for the crazy wizard over the modern scientist. Things we would decry in this world can be positive courses of action in game. There are ways of handling Climate change so that it resists change, it might be a widespread paradox or a hypernarrative. But if convincing the populace that Climate Change isn't happening makes it stops, that also works. Mage isn't our world, it's supposed to be stranger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox is another interesting factor. If reality is defined by the Consensus, then Paradox is, too. So in a world that's purely subjective, nothing accepted by the Consensus can cause Paradox. OTOH, if it's possible for the Consensus to be <i>wrong</i>, then it's entirely possible for something that's part of the Consensus to cause Paradox.<br /> <br /> I'll grant the Hypernarratives thing, with the caveat that both Hypernarratives and Mythic Threads can only exist in a Consensus where minority views can also potentially influence reality. Which, again, means that the Consensus can be wrong (in the sense that it can produce inconsistent results such that what the majority believes doesn't always match what actually happens).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-12-2016, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T09:00:52-07:00","id":986168,"title":"","content":"Changing the past is something that even unenlighted victorious men did.<br /> The past might not literally be rewritten, but what is the difference really?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T10:29:29-07:00","id":986211,"title":"","content":"If all you do is to change the <i>records</i> of the past, and not the actual past, the things about which you sought to make people forget have a nasty tendency to resurface in the present. If you <i>actually change history</i>, then there's nothing forgotten to return. Deny the Holocaust to the point that it never actually happened, and the nation of Israel disappears, whereas the Jewish population in Europe suddenly skyrockets. Or did you think that altering the past wouldn't change the present?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:17:13-07:00","id":986234,"title":"","content":"Altering the past should not lead to subjective changes.<br /> <br /> Because your past is changed as well.<br /> <br /> The only thing that can get changed is the interpretation of the past.<br /> <br /> Forgotten things that resurface are manageable. Undermine credibility for starters.<br /> <br /> Record changing is much easier and completely without risk of paradox.<br /> And on top changed history can also be reverted...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:28:14-07:00","id":986246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=986151#post986151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new Roman\">\u201cAll animals are equal; but some are more equal than others.\u201d \u2014 <i>Animal Farm</i></span></div>Right here, you're tacitly admitting that reality <i>isn't</i> entirely subjective, and that it's possible for there to be a disconnect between the Consensus and Reality \u2014 that is, it's possible for the Consensus to be wrong. Which is what I'm saying. I'm not arguing that the Consensus doesn't <i>influence</i> reality in the world of <b>Mage</b> or that reality doesn't have subjective elements to it; it obviously does, and the Traditions are not wrong point out that belief can change reality. But they <i>are</i> wrong to the extent that they say that reality is entirely a product of the Consensus except when overruled by Enlightened Will. Likewise, the Technocracy isn't wrong to point out that there <i>are</i> things that don't depend on the Consensus to exist; and it may even be right that Technocratic Reality Zones are closer to the default reality that would exist if Willworking (including the collective Willworking of the Consensus) wasn't a factor. It <i>is</i> wrong, and blatantly so, to the extent that it argues that Superstitionists don't have real power and are delusional. The truth of the matter is that reality is neither entirely subjective nor entirely objective; rather, it exists as an uneasy mix of the two.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was mostly just aiming for a pithy quote. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> I fully admit a few things have to be objective, but I don't see that as a barrier to a world where the vast majority (or even all) of what people experience and interact with is determined by the consensus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=986151#post986151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That last caveat is key. Also key is the question of who gets to vote. <b>Mage</b> posits the notion that beings with Avatars have the ability to Willwork, and that beings without Avatars don't. And with the possible exception of the Celestial Chorus' Pure Ones and the Taft\u00e2ni's Djinn, <b>Mage</b> further posits that only humans have Avatars. That means that vampires, werewolves, spirits, and ghosts don't get a vote in the Consensus. Sure, you could argue that there are entities with Avatar-like reality-warping abilities who serve as \u201csponsors\u201d for these beings otherwise have no say in the Consensus; but as soon as you say that, you're redefining what the Consensus is generally understood to mean: it's longer the collective Willworking of humanity's Sleeper population, but rather it's that plus the X-factor of \u201cthe Will of God\u201d or whatever term you wish to apply to the inhuman entities who cause reality to frequently deviate from what the collective beliefs of humanity say it is. And since this X-factor is essentially unknowable, \u201cthe Will of God\u201d is largely indistinguishable from \u201cCosmological Constants\u201d. Do spirits exist as they do because the Triat believes in them, or is it because they're an intrinsic part of reality that can't be expunged by human disbelief (as opposed to the Bygones)? Who knows? What we <i>do</i> know is that spirits aren't subject to the \u201cI don't believe in fairies\u201d phenomenon the way that dragons and unicorns are.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want a Will of God in Mage that isn't actually subservient to the Consensus (and yes, if I actually want to bring it into Mage, I do) you do have to invoke Cosmological Constants. Or you have to say the world is stranger than anyone understands, which pretty much amounts to the same thing.<br /> <br /> Oddly enough, when I was looking for quotes earlier, I found a line in M2nd that said Spirits did contribute to the consensus. I suspect that's a concept that's been dropped over the years, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=986151#post986151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that the current population of the world dwarfs the entire accumulated population of the world from the dawn of time to, what, the 19th century? you again need something more involved than \u201cmajority rules\u201d to keep the present Consensus from overriding the past. Admittedly, the Holocaust is more recent than that; but then, it wasn't until the end of WWII that it became public knowledge; so the population that you need to override to get rid of it is limited to a little more than the past seven decades of humanity. A tough hurdle, but not necessarily an insurmountable one if you can extend the population explosion (say, by colonizing Space). The point is that you need something more involved than \u201creality is subjective\u201d to keep the promotion of Holocaust Denial from being a viable tactic for retroactively eliminating the Holocaust.</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking the emotional weight of a specific historic event out for a second, it would be a damn cool story element if the Technocracy was literally rewriting the past by convincing the modern populace that certain things did or did not happen. I've actually pondered that as a potential front in the Ascension War before. There is enormous potential in exploring how consensual reality and time interact. That said, it gets very complicated, and there are any number of permutations depending on how many different pasts can exist at once, how much they affect the present, whether the future is written yet or not. That's probably why Mage takes a blunt instrument to the idea of Time Travel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=986211#post986211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If all you do is to change the <i>records</i> of the past, and not the actual past, the things about which you sought to make people forget have a nasty tendency to resurface in the present. If you <i>actually change history</i>, then there's nothing forgotten to return. Deny the Holocaust to the point that it never actually happened, and the nation of Israel disappears, whereas the Jewish population in Europe suddenly skyrockets. Or did you think that altering the past wouldn't change the present?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, now I see where you are coming from. While I'm not going to outright deny that the Consensus could theoretically make drastic, sudden, and visible changes to reality, I will ask: Where do you even start? That is one hell of a change and the fact that time manipulation was involved doesn't make it any less alien to the minds of the sleepers. They are going to strongly resist that change unless you also convince them that the present is different too. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Paradox is another interesting factor. If reality is defined by the Consensus, then Paradox is, too. So in a world that's purely subjective, nothing accepted by the Consensus can cause Paradox. OTOH, if it's possible for the Consensus to be <i>wrong</i>, then it's entirely possible for something that's part of the Consensus to cause Paradox.<br /> <br /> I'll grant the Hypernarratives thing, with the caveat that both Hypernarratives and Mythic Threads can only exist in a Consensus where minority views can also potentially influence reality. Which, again, means that the Consensus can be wrong (in the sense that it can produce inconsistent results such that what the majority believes doesn't always match what actually happens). </div> </div> </div>I think we are in agreement that simple majority rule is a terrible way to run the Consensus. Also, if that is what you are going for by the consensus being wrong, I'll concede that right now. We already have examples of how the Consensus isn't consistent, both in how much play there is in the line between possible and impossible, and in the way the Scourge used to work.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T13:45:56-07:00","id":986359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=986246#post986246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was mostly just aiming for a pithy quote. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I fully admit a few things have to be objective, but I don't see that as a barrier to a world where the vast majority (or even all) of what people experience and interact with is determined by the consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Change \u201cdetermined by\u201d to \u201cinfluenced by\u201d, and we're in full agreement. The distinction being whether there are other factors at play that allows for some dissonance between what \u201ceveryone knows\u201d to be true and what actually is true \u2014 that is, whether or not the Consensus can be wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=986246#post986246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want a Will of God in Mage that isn't actually subservient to the Consensus (and yes, if I actually want to bring it into Mage, I do) you do have to invoke Cosmological Constants. Or you have to say the world is stranger than anyone understands, which pretty much amounts to the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you have to say that the Godhead has an ability to shape reality that's <i>at least</i> on par with what the most powerful Archmages can manage, and probably beyond even that, and that He/She/It/They exercise Their Will to impose some order on the cosmos.<br /> <br /> Which, in practice, is just another way of saying Cosmological Constants. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=986246#post986246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oddly enough, when I was looking for quotes earlier, I found a line in M2nd that said Spirits did contribute to the consensus. I suspect that's a concept that's been dropped over the years, though.</div> </div> </div> </div> Interesting. For the record, could you provide a page reference?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=986246#post986246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking the emotional weight of a specific historic event out for a second, it would be a damn cool story element if the Technocracy was literally rewriting the past by convincing the modern populace that certain things did or did not happen. I've actually pondered that as a potential front in the Ascension War before. There is enormous potential in exploring how consensual reality and time interact. That said, it gets very complicated, and there are any number of permutations depending on how many different pasts can exist at once, how much they affect the present, whether the future is written yet or not. That's probably why Mage takes a blunt instrument to the idea of Time Travel.</div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>would</i> be a cool story idea, with proper constraints. The way I'd handle it would be to allow the NWO to use \u201cthe Masses\u201d (or rather, propaganda) as an instrument in their Willworking, adding Mind and maybe Data to a Time Effect to alter history by rewriting the proverbial history books. That's a far cry from using <i>just</i> propaganda, with no Enlightened Will backing it up, to alter history, which is what I was arguing should be possible if the Consensus truly determined everything \u2014 and which, by the absurdity of it, I was presenting as an argument as to why the Consensus <i>can't</i> be determining everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=986246#post986246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, now I see where you are coming from. While I'm not going to outright deny that the Consensus could theoretically make drastic, sudden, and visible changes to reality, I will ask: Where do you even start? That is one hell of a change and the fact that time manipulation was involved doesn't make it any less alien to the minds of the sleepers. They are going to strongly resist that change unless you also convince them that the present is different too.</div> </div> </div> </div> If they retroactively change the past, who's to say they'll notice the changes to the present? Or rather, who's to say that anyone will realize that the present used to be different? This is an admittedly strained argument; but then, as I just said above, I don't actually consider the notion that the modern Consensus has that much influence over the past to be a reasonable one. I just think that it's a necessary corollary to saying that reality is entirely subjective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=986246#post986246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we are in agreement that simple majority rule is a terrible way to run the Consensus. Also, if that is what you are going for by the consensus being wrong, I'll concede that right now. We already have examples of how the Consensus isn't consistent, both in how much play there is in the line between possible and impossible, and in the way the Scourge used to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much.<br /> <br /> With all that said, let me add a caveat: I think a lot of the problems of a purely subjective reality can be mitigated it you apply a few hard rules to <i>how</i> belief shapes reality. First and foremost, it is <i>not</i> \u201cone man, one vote\u201d. Even setting aside \u201cWill of God\u201d/Cosmological Constants for the moment, a single mage has enough influence to override the local Sleepers on his own. Next, without worldwide Sphere knowledge, separation mitigates one's influence over reality, and this applies least as much to Sleepers as of does to the Awakened. Reality Zones are the result of Sleepers not being able to transcend space (though the Internet may be changing this). Historical Inertia may be rooted in the fact that it's much easier to influence the future than it is to influence the past. And the \u201cWild West\u201d nature of the Umbra may be the result of it being isolated from most of the Avatar-bearing population (read: \u201chumans\u201d) by the Gauntlet. Add to that some potent \u201cminority lobbies\u201d (I.e., Mythic Threads), and I'll agree that the Consensus can do a lot.<br /> <br /> But not everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-12-2016, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T14:29:35-07:00","id":986384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=986060#post986060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it is one of the primary weaknesses of any subjective philosophy. It eventually devolves to a narcissist fantasy because you can set reality by wishing really, really hard. It just works out better, from a philosophical point of view, if all Mages are lunatics whose perceptions are altered by their Avatars to fit their paradigms (Marauders have just stumbled on the ability to externality their lunacy).</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't go that far. I'm saying that reality isn't fundamentally subjective, even in <b>Mage</b>. But a fundamental conceit of the game is that reality <i>is</i> subject, to some extent, to the wishes of beings with Avatars (the key being \u201cto some extent\u201d); so <b>Mage</b>'s reality isn't fundamentally <i>objective</i>, either; not in a practical sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T14:32:13-07:00","id":986388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=986359#post986359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It would be a cool story idea, with proper constraints. The way I'd handle it would be to allow the NWO to use \u201cthe Masses\u201d (or rather, propaganda) as an instrument in their Willworking, adding Mind and maybe Data to a Time Effect to alter history by rewriting the proverbial history books. That's a far cry from using just propaganda, with no Enlightened Will backing it up, to alter history, which is what I was arguing should be possible if the Consensus truly determined everything \u2014 and which, by the absurdity of it, I was presenting as an argument as to why the Consensus can't be determining everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Altough it sounds absurd, and I don't think propaganda alone should be sufficient to change the past.<br /> The difference between change and the illusion of change is very minor.<br /> Sure a mage can tell the difference using various ways. But regardless if the false past gets real \u201cby the power of the consensus\u201c or not, if the enginered past doesn't contradict the present...<br /> <br /> Adding the notion that magick gets coloured by the user up to and including sensory and scrying effects.<br /> (Of course it was THEM)<br /> <br /> Presto!<br /> The past is changed without being changed.<br /> (My truth, my will, my consensus! *puttingdownthreepictures*)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12022,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","user":"Nonsense","date":".  Typo 10-12-2016, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T12:49:51-07:00","id":986899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=986359#post986359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Change \u201cdetermined by\u201d to \u201cinfluenced by\u201d, and we're in full agreement. The distinction being whether there are other factors at play that allows for some dissonance between what \u201ceveryone knows\u201d to be true and what actually is true \u2014 that is, whether or not the Consensus can be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm having a hard time explaining my objection to this without splitting hairs. The best I can explain it is that 'influenced by' does not carry the weight I think the Consensus can have. 'Largely determined by' would be better, as it shows what the Consensus can do if nothing else is interfering, while leaving open the possibility of conflict.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=986359#post986359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. For the record, could you provide a page reference?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure thing. Page 67<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage 2nd Edition, Page 67</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, humanity is not the only participant in this cosmic dance. Spirits from the Umbrae or other realities may well influence our own world through their consciousness, beliefs and paradigms. The Dreamspeakers and Verbena often speak of how animal and plant spirits add their voices to the world's song, while the Virtual Adepts insist that techno-spirits influence the spread of the world wide computer web.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=986359#post986359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It <i>would</i> be a cool story idea, with proper constraints. The way I'd handle it would be to allow the NWO to use \u201cthe Masses\u201d (or rather, propaganda) as an instrument in their Willworking, adding Mind and maybe Data to a Time Effect to alter history by rewriting the proverbial history books. That's a far cry from using <i>just</i> propaganda, with no Enlightened Will backing it up, to alter history, which is what I was arguing should be possible if the Consensus truly determined everything \u2014 and which, by the absurdity of it, I was presenting as an argument as to why the Consensus <i>can't</i> be determining everything.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they retroactively change the past, who's to say they'll notice the changes to the present? Or rather, who's to say that anyone will realize that the present used to be different? This is an admittedly strained argument; but then, as I just said above, I don't actually consider the notion that the modern Consensus has that much influence over the past to be a reasonable one. I just think that it's a necessary corollary to saying that reality is entirely subjective. </div> </div> </div>So, a bootstrap paradox then? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The problem with Time Travel examples is there are too many ways of resolving them and not enough information to say which one is correct. So the absurdity seems more like standard temporal fare and less like a problem with the Consensus itself. Were I to run a game where the consensus could alter the past, I would still only let that change the present in mostly unnoticable ways. Disappearing a country isn't going to happen. Creating the ruins of an ancient civilization in out of the way places? That might work. <br /> <br /> For the record, I do agree that there have to be some restrictions on how the Consensus works and indeed I put two into place earlier to avoid a couple of major contraditions I've run into over the years. However, I find two or three Constants takes Mage almost entirely into the realm we expect it to be in while keeping the possibilities almost endless.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/967358-magick-question-what-happens-when-the-consensus-is-wrong?p=986359#post986359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much.<br /> <br /> With all that said, let me add a caveat: I think a lot of the problems of a purely subjective reality can be mitigated it you apply a few hard rules to <i>how</i> belief shapes reality. First and foremost, it is <i>not</i> \u201cone man, one vote\u201d. Even setting aside \u201cWill of God\u201d/Cosmological Constants for the moment, a single mage has enough influence to override the local Sleepers on his own. Next, without worldwide Sphere knowledge, separation mitigates one's influence over reality, and this applies least as much to Sleepers as of does to the Awakened. Reality Zones are the result of Sleepers not being able to transcend space (though the Internet may be changing this). Historical Inertia may be rooted in the fact that it's much easier to influence the future than it is to influence the past. And the \u201cWild West\u201d nature of the Umbra may be the result of it being isolated from most of the Avatar-bearing population (read: \u201chumans\u201d) by the Gauntlet. Add to that some potent \u201cminority lobbies\u201d (I.e., Mythic Threads), and I'll agree that the Consensus can do a lot.<br /> <br /> But not everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I pretty much accept all of that. I suspect we'll find a few places places we disagree if we get into the details, although a lot of that might be semantics (e.g. impossible vs theoretically possible but never going to happen). <br /> <br /> In general, I like Mage to be a strange game that keeps us questioning our assumptions about what the world even is. One that pulls the rug out from under us every time we think we know how things work. Expecting rules but finding none (or expecting none and finding them anyways) contributes to that classic feel of Reality on the Brink that sets Mage apart.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}